ion":957,"supportScope":"Topic/format lineage only; not evidence for the new factual claim"}],"explanation74":"Etruria lay chiefly in present-day Tuscany, western Umbria and northern Lazio.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0031","nodeId":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0031","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The Chernobyl nuclear disaster occurred in a republic then belonging to the:","value":"Soviet Union","group":"Alpha coverage extension","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[{"file":"AlphaTest source-concept lineage","sourceQuestion":302,"supportScope":"Topic/format lineage only; not evidence for the new factual claim"}],"explanation74":"Chernobyl was in the Ukrainian Soviet Socialist Republic when the disaster occurred in 1986.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0032","nodeId":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0032","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The Edict of Nantes sought primarily to regulate the position of which group?","value":"French Protestants","group":"Alpha coverage extension","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[{"file":"AlphaTest source-concept lineage","sourceQuestion":453,"supportScope":"Topic/format lineage only; not evidence for the new factual claim"}],"explanation74":"Henry IV granted French Protestants limited protections after the Wars of Religion.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0033","nodeId":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0033","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The Duma established after the Russian Revolution of 1905 was a:","value":"Representative assembly","group":"Alpha coverage extension","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[{"file":"AlphaTest source-concept lineage","sourceQuestion":212,"supportScope":"Topic/format lineage only; not evidence for the new factual claim"}],"explanation74":"The Duma was an elected legislative assembly, though the tsar retained extensive powers.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0034","nodeId":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0034","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The Weimar Republic was the name given to Germany's political system between:","value":"The First World War and Nazi rule","group":"Alpha coverage extension","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[{"file":"AlphaTest source-concept lineage","sourceQuestion":90,"supportScope":"Topic/format lineage only; not evidence for the new factual claim"}],"explanation74":"The republic followed Germany's defeat in 1918 and ended with the Nazi consolidation of power.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0035","nodeId":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0035","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The Roman Lares were connected chiefly with:","value":"Domestic and local protection","group":"Alpha coverage extension","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[{"file":"AlphaTest source-concept lineage","sourceQuestion":420,"supportScope":"Topic/format lineage only; not evidence for the new factual claim"}],"explanation74":"Lares were protective deities associated with households, neighbourhoods and places.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0036","nodeId":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0036","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The Columbian Exchange refers to transfers of plants, animals and diseases between:","value":"The Americas and the Old World","group":"Alpha coverage extension","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[{"file":"AlphaTest source-concept lineage","sourceQuestion":169,"supportScope":"Topic/format lineage only; not evidence for the new factual claim"}],"explanation74":"Contact after 1492 reshaped agriculture, populations and ecosystems on both sides of the Atlantic.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0049","nodeId":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0049","anchor":"MAJOR:GEOGRAPHY-AND-CIVICS","subject":"The Azores are an autonomous region of:","value":"Portugal","group":"Alpha coverage extension","major":"Geography & Civics","relation":"review question","references":[{"file":"AlphaTest source-concept lineage","sourceQuestion":428,"supportScope":"Topic/format lineage only; not evidence for the new factual claim"}],"explanation74":"The Azores are a Portuguese archipelago in the North Atlantic.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0050","nodeId":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0050","anchor":"MAJOR:GEOGRAPHY-AND-CIVICS","subject":"The Canary Islands belong to which country?","value":"Spain","group":"Alpha coverage extension","major":"Geography & Civics","relation":"review question","references":[{"file":"AlphaTest source-concept lineage","sourceQuestion":428,"supportScope":"Topic/format lineage only; not evidence for the new factual claim"}],"explanation74":"The Canaries are Spanish, although geographically off the northwestern coast of Africa.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0051","nodeId":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0051","anchor":"MAJOR:GEOGRAPHY-AND-CIVICS","subject":"The Republic of Ireland shares its only land border with which sovereign state?","value":"United Kingdom","group":"Alpha coverage extension","major":"Geography & Civics","relation":"review question","references":[{"file":"AlphaTest source-concept lineage","sourceQuestion":428,"supportScope":"Topic/format lineage only; not evidence for the new factual claim"}],"explanation74":"The border separates the Republic of Ireland from Northern Ireland, which is part of the United Kingdom.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0052","nodeId":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0052","anchor":"MAJOR:GEOGRAPHY-AND-CIVICS","subject":"Which currency is used in Switzerland?","value":"Swiss franc","group":"Alpha coverage extension","major":"Geography & Civics","relation":"review question","references":[{"file":"AlphaTest source-concept lineage","sourceQuestion":438,"supportScope":"Topic/format lineage only; not evidence for the new factual claim"}],"explanation74":"Switzerland uses the Swiss franc and is not a member of the euro area.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0053","nodeId":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0053","anchor":"MAJOR:GEOGRAPHY-AND-CIVICS","subject":"A tariff imposed on imported goods is a:","value":"Customs duty","group":"Alpha coverage extension","major":"Geography & Civics","relation":"review question","references":[{"file":"AlphaTest source-concept lineage","sourceQuestion":224,"supportScope":"Topic/format lineage only; not evidence for the new factual claim"}],"explanation74":"Import tariffs tax goods entering a country and can raise their domestic price.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0055","nodeId":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0055","anchor":"MAJOR:GEOGRAPHY-AND-CIVICS","subject":"Lake Geneva lies on the border between Switzerland and:","value":"France","group":"Alpha coverage extension","major":"Geography & Civics","relation":"review question","references":[{"file":"AlphaTest source-concept lineage","sourceQuestion":392,"supportScope":"Topic/format lineage only; not evidence for the new factual claim"}],"explanation74":"The lake, also called Lac Léman, has Swiss and French shores.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0056","nodeId":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0056","anchor":"MAJOR:GEOGRAPHY-AND-CIVICS","subject":"The Strait of Hormuz connects the Persian Gulf with the:","value":"Gulf of Oman","group":"Alpha coverage extension","major":"Geography & Civics","relation":"review question","references":[{"file":"AlphaTest source-concept lineage","sourceQuestion":619,"supportScope":"Topic/format lineage only; not evidence for the new factual claim"}],"explanation74":"The strait is the narrow maritime connection between the Persian Gulf and Gulf of Oman.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0057","nodeId":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0057","anchor":"MAJOR:GEOGRAPHY-AND-CIVICS","subject":"Which of these crops is traditionally associated with the Mediterranean climate?","value":"Olive","group":"Alpha coverage extension","major":"Geography & Civics","relation":"review question","references":[{"file":"AlphaTest source-concept lineage","sourceQuestion":169,"supportScope":"Topic/format lineage only; not evidence for the new factual claim"}],"explanation74":"Olives are adapted to Mediterranean summers that are hot and relatively dry.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0058","nodeId":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0058","anchor":"MAJOR:GEOGRAPHY-AND-CIVICS","subject":"Corsica belongs to which country?","value":"France","group":"Alpha coverage extension","major":"Geography & Civics","relation":"review question","references":[{"file":"AlphaTest source-concept lineage","sourceQuestion":428,"supportScope":"Topic/format lineage only; not evidence for the new factual claim"}],"explanation74":"Corsica is French; nearby Sardinia is Italian.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0059","nodeId":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0059","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The medieval Hanseatic League was primarily an association of:","value":"Trading towns","group":"Alpha coverage extension","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[{"file":"AlphaTest source-concept lineage","sourceQuestion":103,"supportScope":"Topic/format lineage only; not evidence for the new factual claim"}],"explanation74":"North European towns cooperated to protect trade, especially around the Baltic and North Sea.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0061","nodeId":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0061","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The Palazzo Pubblico and Piazza del Campo are closely associated with which Italian city-state?","value":"Siena","group":"Alpha coverage extension","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[{"file":"AlphaTest source-concept lineage","sourceQuestion":230,"supportScope":"Topic/format lineage only; not evidence for the new factual claim"}],"explanation74":"Siena's civic centre reflects the political and commercial life of the medieval commune.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0062","nodeId":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0062","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The Thirty Years' War began in which region of the Holy Roman Empire?","value":"Bohemia","group":"Alpha coverage extension","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[{"file":"AlphaTest source-concept lineage","sourceQuestion":453,"supportScope":"Topic/format lineage only; not evidence for the new factual claim"}],"explanation74":"The Bohemian revolt and the Prague defenestration helped trigger the conflict.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0063","nodeId":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0063","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The principle cuius regio, eius religio concerned the relationship between a ruler and the territory's:","value":"Religion","group":"Alpha coverage extension","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[{"file":"AlphaTest source-concept lineage","sourceQuestion":453,"supportScope":"Topic/format lineage only; not evidence for the new factual claim"}],"explanation74":"The ruler's confession determined the territory's official religion under the Augsburg settlement, subject to its limitations.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0064","nodeId":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0064","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The Janissaries were an elite military corps of the:","value":"Ottoman Empire","group":"Alpha coverage extension","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[{"file":"AlphaTest source-concept lineage","sourceQuestion":198,"supportScope":"Topic/format lineage only; not evidence for the new factual claim"}],"explanation74":"Janissaries formed a major infantry institution in the Ottoman state.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0065","nodeId":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0065","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which Roman title denoted the two annually elected chief magistrates of the Republic?","value":"Consuls","group":"Alpha coverage extension","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[{"file":"AlphaTest source-concept lineage","sourceQuestion":420,"supportScope":"Topic/format lineage only; not evidence for the new factual claim"}],"explanation74":"Two consuls held the republic's highest regular magistracy, limiting concentration of authority in one person.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0066","nodeId":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0066","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The Roman office of censor was associated with the census and oversight of:","value":"Public morals","group":"Alpha coverage extension","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[{"file":"AlphaTest source-concept lineage","sourceQuestion":307,"supportScope":"Topic/format lineage only; not evidence for the new factual claim"}],"explanation74":"Censors registered citizens and exercised supervisory powers over public conduct and standing.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0067","nodeId":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0067","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The Roman policy described as panem et circenses referred to food distributions and:","value":"Public spectacles","group":"Alpha coverage extension","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[{"file":"AlphaTest source-concept lineage","sourceQuestion":169,"supportScope":"Topic/format lineage only; not evidence for the new factual claim"}],"explanation74":"The phrase links grain provision and entertainment with popular political acquiescence.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0068","nodeId":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0068","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Lenin’s New Economic Policy allowed a limited revival of:","value":"Private trade","group":"Alpha coverage extension","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[{"file":"AlphaTest source-concept lineage","sourceQuestion":212,"supportScope":"Topic/format lineage only; not evidence for the new factual claim"}],"explanation74":"The NEP permitted some market activity while the state retained major sectors of the economy.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0069","nodeId":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0069","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The Nuremberg Laws of 1935 concerned chiefly:","value":"Racial citizenship and marriage restrictions","group":"Alpha coverage extension","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[{"file":"AlphaTest source-concept lineage","sourceQuestion":90,"supportScope":"Topic/format lineage only; not evidence for the new factual claim"}],"explanation74":"The laws deprived Jews of citizenship rights and imposed racist restrictions on marriage and relations.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0070","nodeId":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0070","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The policy of appeasement is particularly associated with European diplomacy towards:","value":"Nazi Germany","group":"Alpha coverage extension","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[{"file":"AlphaTest source-concept lineage","sourceQuestion":90,"supportScope":"Topic/format lineage only; not evidence for the new factual claim"}],"explanation74":"In the late 1930s, concessions were made in the hope of avoiding another European war.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0071","nodeId":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0071","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The Bretton Woods conference established a framework for international monetary cooperation near the end of the:","value":"Second World War","group":"Alpha coverage extension","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[{"file":"AlphaTest source-concept lineage","sourceQuestion":224,"supportScope":"Topic/format lineage only; not evidence for the new factual claim"}],"explanation74":"The 1944 conference laid foundations for post-war financial institutions and monetary arrangements.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0072","nodeId":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0072","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The Dreyfus Affair exposed deep divisions in French society over justice and:","value":"Antisemitism","group":"Alpha coverage extension","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[{"file":"AlphaTest source-concept lineage","sourceQuestion":453,"supportScope":"Topic/format lineage only; not evidence for the new factual claim"}],"explanation74":"A Jewish army officer was wrongly convicted of treason, provoking a major political and moral controversy.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0073","nodeId":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0073","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The term ancien régime usually denotes France’s political order before the:","value":"French Revolution","group":"Alpha coverage extension","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[{"file":"AlphaTest source-concept lineage","sourceQuestion":230,"supportScope":"Topic/format lineage only; not evidence for the new factual claim"}],"explanation74":"It denotes the monarchy and estate-based order challenged by the revolution beginning in 1789.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0074","nodeId":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0074","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"In pre-revolutionary France, the Third Estate comprised chiefly:","value":"Those outside clergy and nobility","group":"Alpha coverage extension","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[{"file":"AlphaTest source-concept lineage","sourceQuestion":230,"supportScope":"Topic/format lineage only; not evidence for the new factual claim"}],"explanation74":"The Third Estate included a wide range of people, from peasants to wealthy bourgeois citizens.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0075","nodeId":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0075","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The Non-Aligned Movement sought to avoid formal alignment with:","value":"The US-led and Soviet-led blocs","group":"Alpha coverage extension","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[{"file":"AlphaTest source-concept lineage","sourceQuestion":619,"supportScope":"Topic/format lineage only; not evidence for the new factual claim"}],"explanation74":"Its members sought room for independent action outside the US–Soviet bloc division.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0076","nodeId":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0076","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The Russian term soviet originally denotes a:","value":"Council","group":"Alpha coverage extension","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[{"file":"AlphaTest source-concept lineage","sourceQuestion":212,"supportScope":"Topic/format lineage only; not evidence for the new factual claim"}],"explanation74":"Soviets were councils, notably of workers and soldiers, during the revolutionary period.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0077","nodeId":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0077","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which American civilization had its capital at Tenochtitlan?","value":"Aztec","group":"Alpha coverage extension","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[{"file":"AlphaTest source-concept lineage","sourceQuestion":169,"supportScope":"Topic/format lineage only; not evidence for the new factual claim"}],"explanation74":"Tenochtitlan stood on the site of present-day Mexico City.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0078","nodeId":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0078","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The Inca Empire's principal centre was:","value":"Cusco","group":"Alpha coverage extension","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[{"file":"AlphaTest source-concept lineage","sourceQuestion":169,"supportScope":"Topic/format lineage only; not evidence for the new factual claim"}],"explanation74":"Cusco in the Andes was the political and ceremonial heart of the Inca state.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0079","nodeId":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0079","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The Roman practice of damnatio memoriae involved an attempt to suppress a person's:","value":"Public memory","group":"Alpha coverage extension","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[{"file":"AlphaTest source-concept lineage","sourceQuestion":307,"supportScope":"Topic/format lineage only; not evidence for the new factual claim"}],"explanation74":"Names and images could be removed or altered to condemn a person's memory.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0080","nodeId":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0080","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"A Renaissance signoria was typically a form of:","value":"Rule by a lord or ruling family","group":"Alpha coverage extension","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[{"file":"AlphaTest source-concept lineage","sourceQuestion":230,"supportScope":"Topic/format lineage only; not evidence for the new factual claim"}],"explanation74":"Several Italian communes came under dominant individual or family rule.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0082","nodeId":"REVIEW98-ARCHED-NEW98-0082","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The term diaspora refers to a population’s:","value":"Dispersion beyond an ancestral homeland","group":"Alpha coverage extension","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[{"file":"AlphaTest source-concept lineage","sourceQuestion":453,"supportScope":"Topic/format lineage only; not evidence for the new factual claim"}],"explanation74":"Diaspora communities live dispersed while retaining connections with a homeland or shared origin.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0001","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0001","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What did the Grand Tour offer young European elites?","value":"Travel for cultural education","group":"Intellectual Context","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Italy's antiquities, cities and collections were major destinations.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0002","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0002","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Venetian square forms the ceremonial setting of the basilica and doge's palace?","value":"Piazza San Marco","group":"Urban Spaces","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its architecture concentrates religious and political institutions.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0003","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0003","anchor":"MAJOR:LANGUAGE-AND-LITERATURE","subject":"Which composer developed the twelve-tone method associated with the Second Viennese School?","value":"Arnold Schoenberg","group":"Composers","major":"Language & Literature","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The method organises the twelve pitch classes in a structured series.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0004","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0004","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Le Corbusier book compared modern engineering with the renewal of architecture?","value":"Towards a New Architecture","group":"Architectural Books","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its arguments linked architectural form with the conditions of modern life.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0005","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0005","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which porous carbonate stone is strongly associated with Roman building façades and quarries near Tivoli?","value":"Travertine","group":"Stone Materials","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It forms through mineral deposition from water.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0006","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0006","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"What is a proposed explanation that can be tested against evidence called?","value":"Hypothesis","group":"Scientific Methods","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"A scientific hypothesis must allow meaningful comparison with observations.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0007","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0007","anchor":"MAJOR:LANGUAGE-AND-LITERATURE","subject":"Which Italian actress played Gelsomina in La strada?","value":"Giulietta Masina","group":"Cultural Figures","major":"Language & Literature","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Her expressive performance is central to the film's emotional character.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0008","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0008","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which term describes a crop grown mainly for sale?","value":"cash crop","group":"Trade Economics","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its production depends on market demand rather than only household needs.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0009","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0009","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes a venue for horse or chariot racing in the ancient Greek and Byzantine world?","value":"Hippodrome","group":"Urban","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its elongated track suited racing events.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0011","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0011","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"A building organised around an open internal court has which plan type?","value":"Courtyard plan","group":"Plan Types","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The court can provide light, ventilation and controlled outdoor space.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0014","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0014","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which drawing enlarges a junction to explain construction?","value":"Detail drawing","group":"Architectural Drawing","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It gives information that cannot be read clearly at the building scale.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0015","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0015","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which building type served the communal government of medieval Italian cities?","value":"Palazzo comunale","group":"Historic Types","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its placement and form represented civic authority.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0017","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0017","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which movement advocated workers' organisation through trade unions as an agent of revolutionary change?","value":"Revolutionary syndicalism","group":"Social Movements","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It placed direct economic action at the centre of strategy.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0018","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0018","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Trieste-area castle was built for Archduke Ferdinand Maximilian beside the sea?","value":"Miramare Castle","group":"Italian Castles","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The residence combines a historicist design with a landscaped coastal setting.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0019","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0019","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes the spacing between adjacent columns?","value":"Intercolumniation","group":"Classical","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It affects both structural rhythm and the appearance of a colonnade.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0021","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0021","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which historian examined the conflict between Athens and Sparta?","value":"Thucydides","group":"Greek People","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"His history analyses the Peloponnesian War rather than the Persian Wars.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0022","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0022","anchor":"MAJOR:DESIGN","subject":"Which technique forms a curved piece by bonding multiple thin strips around a mould?","value":"Bent lamination","group":"Woodwork","major":"Design","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The glued layers retain the intended curve after release.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0024","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0024","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which king fought the Hittites at Kadesh?","value":"Ramesses II","group":"Ancient Rulers","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The later Egyptian–Hittite treaty is an important ancient diplomatic document.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0025","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0025","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which Chinese dynasty commissioned much of the surviving Great Wall's brick-and-stone form?","value":"Ming dynasty","group":"World Culture","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The wall comprises constructions from several periods rather than a single project.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0026","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0026","anchor":"MAJOR:DESIGN","subject":"Which early twentieth-century tendency joined luxury materials with geometric ornament?","value":"Art Deco","group":"Design Movements","major":"Design","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its forms appeared in buildings, interiors, objects and graphics.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0027","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0027","anchor":"MAJOR:DESIGN","subject":"Which joint interlocks a shaped projection with a corresponding socket?","value":"Mortise-and-tenon joint","group":"Woodwork","major":"Design","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It is widely used in traditional furniture and timber construction.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0028","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0028","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which battle enabled Saladin to capture much of the Crusader leadership before retaking Jerusalem?","value":"Hattin","group":"Medieval Battles","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The defeat severely weakened the Kingdom of Jerusalem.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0030","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0030","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What was a salon in eighteenth-century intellectual life?","value":"A hosted gathering for conversation","group":"Intellectual Context","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Salons connected literary, philosophical and social networks.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0031","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0031","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which broad, low pointed arch commonly has four centres and appears in late English Gothic?","value":"Tudor arch","group":"Arch Types","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its flattened profile differs from a steep two-centred pointed arch.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0032","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0032","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which dynasty ruled the eastern Islamic world after overthrowing the Umayyads?","value":"Abbasids","group":"Medieval Dynasties","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Their capital at Baghdad became a major imperial centre.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0033","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0033","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Sicilian city contains the historic district of Ibla, extensively rebuilt after the 1693 earthquake?","value":"Ragusa","group":"Italian Urban History","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The lower old town preserves an important Baroque urban landscape.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0036","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0036","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which central Italian cathedral is famous for a façade with mosaics and reliefs by Lorenzo Maitani's workshop?","value":"Orvieto Cathedral","group":"Church Features","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its façade combines sculpture, mosaic and architectural articulation.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0037","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0037","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"What is a 'giardino segreto'?","value":"An enclosed private garden","group":"Landscape Forms","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its separation creates a more intimate space within a larger estate.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0038","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0038","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which dynasty included Charlemagne and Louis the Pious?","value":"Carolingians","group":"Medieval Dynasties","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its rulers shaped the early medieval western empire.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0039","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0039","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which metamorphic stone was widely used for classical and Renaissance sculpture?","value":"Marble","group":"Stone Materials","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its crystalline structure results from the transformation of carbonate rock.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0040","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0040","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"What is the persistence of sound caused by repeated reflections in a room called?","value":"Reverberation","group":"Light Sound","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It differs from a clearly separated single echo.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0041","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0041","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Turin hilltop basilica was built by Juvarra as a dynastic and votive monument?","value":"Superga","group":"Baroque Buildings","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[{"file":"Map record","verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Basilica_of_Superga","verificationStatus":"inherited_reference_locator_not_retrieved_this_pass","supportScope":"Building context; complete question claim still pending verification"}],"explanation74":"Its elevated site makes the church a major landmark.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0043","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0043","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What was a principal objective of Justinian's legal compilation?","value":"Organisation of Roman law","group":"Roman Changes","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The Corpus Juris Civilis influenced later European legal traditions.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0044","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0044","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"What is the group that does not receive an experimental treatment called?","value":"Control group","group":"Scientific Methods","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It provides a basis for comparison with the treated group.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0045","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0045","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"A modern historian's interpretation of an ancient war is usually what kind of source?","value":"Secondary source","group":"Historical Sources","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It analyses earlier evidence rather than originating in the event itself.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0046","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0046","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"What term describes a species introduced outside its natural range that causes ecological harm?","value":"Invasive species","group":"Ecological Terms","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Not every introduced species becomes invasive.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0047","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0047","anchor":"MAJOR:DESIGN","subject":"What is the text of a designed page set into its final visual arrangement called?","value":"Typesetting","group":"Graphic Design","major":"Design","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It includes decisions about type, spacing and line breaks.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0048","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0048","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which empire governed from Cuzco and developed a large Andean road network?","value":"Inca Empire","group":"World Culture","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Roads connected diverse regions under imperial administration.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0049","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0049","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Who is conventionally called the 'father of history'?","value":"Herodotus","group":"Greek People","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"His Histories investigate the background and course of the Greek–Persian conflicts.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0050","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0050","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Roman mosaic technique uses small, regularly cut cubes?","value":"Opus tessellatum","group":"Roman Construction","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The tesserae build patterns and images across the surface.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0052","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0052","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes a private urban house of a prosperous Roman household?","value":"Domus","group":"Urban","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its arrangement commonly included an atrium and reception spaces.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0054","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0054","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What was a principal function of court patronage in Renaissance Italy?","value":"Support of artists and scholars","group":"Renaissance Context","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Patronage also communicated dynastic prestige and political legitimacy.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0055","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0055","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"What is a level outdoor platform attached to or surrounding a building called?","value":"Terrace","group":"Spatial Terms","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It extends usable space into the exterior.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0056","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0056","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Vienna boulevard replaced the city's old defensive walls with major public buildings?","value":"Ringstrasse","group":"European Civic Context","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its architecture represents the civic and imperial institutions of the nineteenth century.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0057","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0057","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Parisian cultural centre places brightly coloured services on its exterior?","value":"Centre Pompidou","group":"Contemporary Buildings","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The external service systems help free interior floors for flexible use.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0058","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0058","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which purple imperial stone from ancient Egyptian quarries became a symbol of Roman authority?","value":"Porphyry","group":"Stone Materials","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its rarity and colour supported prestigious architectural and sculptural uses.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0059","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0059","anchor":"MAJOR:GEOGRAPHY-AND-CIVICS","subject":"What is a chain or group of islands called?","value":"Archipelago","group":"Landforms","major":"Geography & Civics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The islands may have different geological origins.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0060","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0060","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which dynasty supplied the late medieval dukes Philip the Good and Charles the Bold?","value":"Valois-Burgundy","group":"Medieval Dynasties","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Their territories linked Burgundy with the Low Countries.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0061","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0061","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which French minister worked to strengthen royal authority under Louis XIII?","value":"Cardinal Richelieu","group":"Earlymodern People","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"His policies also sought to limit Habsburg influence in Europe.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0062","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0062","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which Greek thinker was condemned to drink hemlock in Athens?","value":"Socrates","group":"Greek People","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"His trial and death are described in works by Plato.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0063","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0063","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The Portuguese Estado da Índia was centred on control of what?","value":"Maritime trading routes and ports","group":"Exploration","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its network differed from a single continuous territorial empire.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0064","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0064","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What role did the Encyclopédie play in the Enlightenment?","value":"Organisation and dissemination of knowledge","group":"Intellectual Context","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its articles also challenged inherited forms of authority.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0065","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0065","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What is 'appeasement' in the context of 1930s diplomacy?","value":"Concessions intended to avoid conflict","group":"Historical Concepts","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The Munich Agreement became its most debated example.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0066","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0066","anchor":"MAJOR:GEOGRAPHY-AND-CIVICS","subject":"What does a map's scale express?","value":"Map distance relative to ground distance","group":"Map Concepts","major":"Geography & Civics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It determines how much territory can be shown at a given level of detail.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0067","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0067","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What was an Athenian 'ostracism'?","value":"Temporary political exile","group":"Ancient Terms","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Citizens could vote to remove a prominent individual for ten years.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0068","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0068","anchor":"MAJOR:GEOGRAPHY-AND-CIVICS","subject":"In which Italian region is the city of Lecce?","value":"Apulia","group":"Italian Regions","major":"Geography & Civics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The local soft stone supported richly carved Baroque architecture.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0069","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0069","anchor":"MAJOR:LANGUAGE-AND-LITERATURE","subject":"Which work by Simone de Beauvoir examines the social construction of women's subordinate position?","value":"The Second Sex","group":"Books Ideas","major":"Language & Literature","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It connects philosophical analysis with history and social experience.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0070","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0070","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"A researcher changes one factor while holding others constant. What is the deliberately changed factor called?","value":"Independent variable","group":"Scientific Methods","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its effect is measured through a dependent variable.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0071","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0071","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which family gave its name to the Roman gallery containing Bernini's Apollo and Daphne?","value":"Borghese","group":"Renaissance Patronage","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Scipione Borghese assembled an influential collection of ancient and modern works.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0072","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0072","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which Italian maritime city established commercial power through colonies such as Caffa?","value":"Genoa","group":"Mediterranean Trade","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its Black Sea networks connected several trading regions.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0073","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0073","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes a window projecting through a sloping roof?","value":"Dormer","group":"Facade","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its own small roof differentiates it from a flush rooflight.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0074","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0074","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which military alliance was established by the North Atlantic Treaty?","value":"NATO","group":"Modern Institutions","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its founding purpose centred on collective defence.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0075","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0075","anchor":"MAJOR:DESIGN","subject":"What is the empty area around and between graphic elements called?","value":"Negative space","group":"Graphic Design","major":"Design","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It contributes to hierarchy and clarity rather than being merely unused.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0076","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0076","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"In which region was the ancient kingdom of Lydia located?","value":"Anatolia","group":"Ancient Places","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Lydia is associated with early coined money.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0077","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0077","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which English chapel is particularly renowned for its broad fan-vaulted ceiling in Cambridge?","value":"King's College Chapel","group":"Gothic Buildings","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The vault is a major achievement of late English Gothic architecture.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0079","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0079","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which missionary is traditionally associated with the conversion of Ireland?","value":"Patrick","group":"Medieval People","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"His historical mission became central to Irish Christian tradition.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0080","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0080","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which battle saw Joan of Arc's campaign help lift an English siege?","value":"Orléans","group":"Medieval Battles","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The relief changed French morale during the Hundred Years' War.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0081","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0081","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which European state retained Greenland as part of its realm after earlier colonial administration?","value":"Denmark","group":"Colonial Powers","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Greenland's political status later developed through expanded self-government.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0082","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0082","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which classical ornament resembles an ox skull?","value":"Bucranium","group":"Architectural Ornament","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It is associated with sacrificial imagery and decorative friezes.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0083","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0083","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"What is 'adaptive reuse'?","value":"Conversion to a new use","group":"Architectural Theory","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The strategy retains an existing building while changing its programme.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0084","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0084","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes a mass projecting from a wall to resist lateral thrust?","value":"Buttress","group":"Structure","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It helps stabilize walls or vault-supporting structures.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0085","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0085","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which event triggered a political crisis after an outspoken socialist deputy was murdered in 1924?","value":"Matteotti assassination","group":"Italian Social History","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The crisis exposed Fascist violence but did not remove Mussolini from power.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0086","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0086","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which French document of 1598 provided limited protections for Huguenots?","value":"Edict of Nantes","group":"Historical Documents","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its later revocation prompted persecution and emigration.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0087","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0087","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What was the principal purpose of a medieval pilgrimage?","value":"Visiting a sacred destination","group":"Medieval Terms","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Routes connected centres such as Rome, Jerusalem and Santiago de Compostela.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0088","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0088","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes the outer facing or covering applied to a building?","value":"Cladding","group":"Construction","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It may provide weather protection and determine external appearance.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0090","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0090","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What was the Prague Spring associated with?","value":"Reform within Czechoslovak socialism","group":"Coldwar Context","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Warsaw Pact intervention ended the reform experiment.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0091","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0091","anchor":"MAJOR:DESIGN","subject":"What is a recognisable graphic mark identifying an organisation or product called?","value":"Logo","group":"Graphic Design","major":"Design","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It forms part of a wider visual identity.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0092","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0092","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes a wall formed with two leaves separated by an air space?","value":"Cavity wall","group":"Construction","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The cavity can help control moisture and improve thermal performance.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0093","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0093","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Le Corbusier proposal envisioned a radically reorganised central Paris with tall towers?","value":"Plan Voisin","group":"Urban Models","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The unbuilt scheme became emblematic of modernist urban reconstruction.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0094","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0094","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which West German chancellor is associated with Ostpolitik?","value":"Willy Brandt","group":"Ww2 People","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The policy sought improved relations with eastern European states.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0095","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0095","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which stone carries parallel inscriptions that helped decipher Egyptian hieroglyphs?","value":"Rosetta Stone","group":"Archaeological Discoveries","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The Greek text provided a key to comparison with Egyptian scripts.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0097","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0097","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Venetian customs building was converted into a contemporary art venue by Tadao Ando?","value":"Punta della Dogana","group":"Architecture Adaptation","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The intervention retained the historic structure while reorganising exhibition space.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0098","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0098","anchor":"MAJOR:LANGUAGE-AND-LITERATURE","subject":"Which director made The Conformist?","value":"Bernardo Bertolucci","group":"Italian Directors","major":"Language & Literature","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The film examines personal conformity and political complicity under Fascism.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0099","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0099","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What was the Directory in revolutionary France?","value":"A five-member executive","group":"Revolution Context","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It governed before Napoleon's coup established the Consulate.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0100","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0100","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What was a principal function of the Index of Prohibited Books?","value":"Regulation of reading by Catholic authorities","group":"Reformation Context","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It identified publications judged unacceptable on religious grounds.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0101","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0101","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes a horizontal member spanning an opening?","value":"Lintel","group":"Structure","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It carries loads above a door, window or similar opening.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0102","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0102","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which movement in nineteenth-century Russia idealised rural communities and sought support among peasants?","value":"Narodnik movement","group":"Social Movements","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its activists debated paths to social transformation outside western industrial models.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0103","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0103","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The Medici family consolidated power in which Renaissance republic?","value":"Florentine Republic","group":"Italian States","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Their influence developed before the later establishment of a hereditary duchy.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0104","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0104","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Padua building contains a great elevated hall above market spaces?","value":"Palazzo della Ragione","group":"Italian Civic Buildings","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The building combined civic and commercial functions.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0105","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0105","anchor":"MAJOR:DESIGN","subject":"What is the distance between successive lines of type called?","value":"Leading","group":"Graphic Design","major":"Design","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It affects readability and the density of a text block.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0107","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0107","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What did the Enlightenment ideal of religious toleration challenge?","value":"Coercion based on belief","group":"Intellectual Context","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Different thinkers proposed different limits to toleration.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0108","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0108","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Munich museum by Leo von Klenze was built to display ancient sculpture?","value":"Glyptothek","group":"European Civic Context","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The building exemplifies the use of classical form for a public art institution.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0109","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0109","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which dynasty's rise began with Osman in northwestern Anatolia?","value":"Ottomans","group":"Medieval Dynasties","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its rulers later conquered Constantinople.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0110","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0110","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"In which region was the ancient city of Corinth located?","value":"Peloponnese","group":"Ancient Places","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its position near the isthmus supported commercial connections.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0111","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0111","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Madrid power-station conversion by Herzog & de Meuron appears to lift its brick volume above the ground?","value":"CaixaForum Madrid","group":"Architecture Adaptation","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The intervention creates a covered public space beneath the retained masonry envelope.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0112","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0112","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"Which London scientific society received a royal charter in the seventeenth century?","value":"Royal Society","group":"Scientific Landmarks","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its activities supported experimental knowledge and scholarly communication.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0113","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0113","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which siege was relieved by forces led by John III Sobieski in 1683?","value":"Vienna","group":"Earlymodern Battles","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The relief checked the Ottoman advance against the Habsburg capital.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0114","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0114","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which ruler's victory at Hastings established Norman rule in England?","value":"William the Conqueror","group":"Medieval People","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The conquest transformed English landholding and government.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0115","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0115","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The Peace of Augsburg addressed coexistence between Catholicism and which confession?","value":"Lutheranism","group":"Religious History","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It did not provide general toleration for every religious group.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0116","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0116","anchor":"MAJOR:GEOGRAPHY-AND-CIVICS","subject":"What is a seasonally dry watercourse in arid regions commonly called?","value":"Wadi","group":"Landforms","major":"Geography & Civics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Sudden rainfall can produce rapid flows within it.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0117","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0117","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which villa near Bagnaia is organised around a descending sequence of water features?","value":"Villa Lante","group":"Italian Villas","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The garden uses water to connect terraces and architectural elements.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0118","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0118","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which papal family is associated with Bernini's patron Pope Urban VIII?","value":"Barberini","group":"Renaissance Patronage","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Their patronage helped shape Baroque Rome.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0119","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0119","anchor":"MAJOR:LANGUAGE-AND-LITERATURE","subject":"Which Italian poet authored La pioggia nel pineto?","value":"Gabriele D'Annunzio","group":"Italian Poets","major":"Language & Literature","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The poem links natural sound with sensory transformation.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0120","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0120","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes a block or articulated masonry element marking a building's external corner?","value":"Quoin","group":"Facade","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Quoins may be structurally or decoratively emphasized.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0121","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0121","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes a chamber beneath a church, often containing tombs or relics?","value":"Crypt","group":"Church","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Crypts are frequently associated with early saints and pilgrimage.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0122","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0122","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What did the Peace of Westphalia add to earlier confessional recognition in the Empire?","value":"Recognition of Calvinism","group":"Reformation Context","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its provisions extended the confessional settlement beyond Catholicism and Lutheranism.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0123","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0123","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"What does 'typology' examine in architecture?","value":"Recurring organisational forms","group":"Architectural Theory","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Types can persist while individual buildings change in style and use.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0124","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0124","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which movement sought a Jewish national homeland and developed politically in late nineteenth-century Europe?","value":"Zionism","group":"Social Movements","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It emerged amid nationalism and antisemitism in different European settings.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0125","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0125","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes a low protective wall at the edge of a roof, terrace or bridge?","value":"Parapet","group":"Facade","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its height and detailing vary with function and period.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0126","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0126","anchor":"MAJOR:LANGUAGE-AND-LITERATURE","subject":"Which American period is associated with directors such as Coppola and Scorsese gaining prominence in the 1970s?","value":"New Hollywood","group":"Cinema Movements","major":"Language & Literature","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Changes in the industry allowed a new generation of filmmakers greater influence.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0127","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0127","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which term describes a market for traded securities?","value":"stock exchange","group":"Trade Economics","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It provides an organised setting for buying and selling shares and other instruments.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0129","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0129","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Roman building converted a domed rotunda into a Christian church in the early Middle Ages?","value":"Pantheon","group":"Ancient Buildings","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[{"file":"Map record","verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pantheon,_Rome","verificationStatus":"inherited_reference_locator_not_retrieved_this_pass","supportScope":"Building context; complete question claim still pending verification"}],"explanation74":"The conversion helped sustain the building's continuing use.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0131","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0131","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Milan former distillery became a major contemporary art foundation complex designed by OMA?","value":"Fondazione Prada","group":"Architecture Adaptation","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The project combines retained industrial buildings with new architectural elements.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0132","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0132","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which battle in 1943 involved a major German offensive against a Soviet salient?","value":"Kursk","group":"Modern Battles","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its outcome strengthened Soviet strategic initiative.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0133","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0133","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which tendency emphasises the visible expression of industrial systems and services?","value":"High-tech architecture","group":"Modern Movements","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Structure and technical equipment often become major compositional elements.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0134","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0134","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which English document of 1689 established limits on royal power after the Glorious Revolution?","value":"Bill of Rights","group":"Historical Documents","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It reinforced the role of Parliament within the constitutional settlement.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0135","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0135","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes an entrance space across the front of a church's nave?","value":"Narthex","group":"Church","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It separates the exterior approach from the main worship space.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0136","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0136","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"A building with a long main axis and parallel aisles has which plan type?","value":"Basilican plan","group":"Plan Types","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The form developed from ancient civic precedents into Christian use.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0137","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0137","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Florentine square fronts the Palazzo Vecchio and contains the Loggia dei Lanzi?","value":"Piazza della Signoria","group":"Urban Spaces","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Sculpture and civic architecture give the space a political character.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0138","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0138","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Venice complex historically concentrated shipbuilding for the republic?","value":"Arsenale","group":"Italian Civic Buildings","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its organisation supported naval and commercial power.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0141","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0141","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which British prime minister signed the Munich Agreement?","value":"Neville Chamberlain","group":"Ww2 People","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The agreement accepted the transfer of the Sudetenland to Germany.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0142","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0142","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which drawing shows a building's external face without perspective convergence?","value":"Elevation","group":"Architectural Drawing","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It records the vertical composition of a façade.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0143","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0143","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What did the abolitionist movement seek to end?","value":"Slavery and the slave trade","group":"Nineteenth Context","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its campaigns took different forms across the Atlantic world.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0145","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0145","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which Prussian king is particularly associated with enlightened absolutism and the Seven Years' War?","value":"Frederick II","group":"Earlymodern People","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"His patronage of culture coexisted with territorial and military ambitions.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0146","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0146","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"What is the spreading of waves around an obstacle or through an opening called?","value":"Diffraction","group":"Light Sound","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The effect depends on the relation between wavelength and obstacle size.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0147","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0147","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which Spanish defeat of a French army in 1808 damaged Napoleon's reputation for invincibility?","value":"Bailén","group":"Napoleonic Battles","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The capitulation encouraged resistance to French occupation.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0148","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0148","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which victory over Austria in 1809 followed the earlier French setback at Aspern-Essling?","value":"Wagram","group":"Napoleonic Battles","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The campaign ended with a new peace imposed on Austria.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0149","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0149","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Pisa cemetery building encloses a long rectangular court beside the cathedral?","value":"Camposanto Monumentale","group":"Italian Civic Buildings","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its arcaded galleries formed a setting for tombs and frescoes.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0150","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0150","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What did Renaissance humanists mean by the studia humanitatis?","value":"Grammar, rhetoric, poetry, history and moral philosophy","group":"Renaissance Context","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The curriculum focused on language and civic formation through classical texts.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0151","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0151","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which North African battle marked a major British victory against Rommel's forces?","value":"El Alamein","group":"Modern Battles","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The victory helped reverse the Axis advance towards Egypt.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0152","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0152","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which repeated angular border pattern is also called a Greek key?","value":"Meander","group":"Architectural Ornament","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The continuous turning line creates a geometric band.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0153","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0153","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The 'October Revolution' brought which political group to power?","value":"Bolsheviks","group":"Revolutions","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"They displaced the Provisional Government in Russia.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0154","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0154","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Venetian building by Sansovino faces the Doge's Palace across the Piazzetta?","value":"Biblioteca Marciana","group":"Italian Civic Buildings","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its classical façade presents learning within a major civic setting.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0155","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0155","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Greek sanctuary was traditionally associated with an oracle of Apollo?","value":"Delphi","group":"Ancient Buildings","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The sanctuary combined religious authority with pan-Hellenic importance.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0156","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0156","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which emperor is associated with a system of four imperial rulers?","value":"Diocletian","group":"Roman People","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The Tetrarchy divided responsibilities among two Augusti and two Caesars.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0157","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0157","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Italian movement is associated with Terragni and a modern language of abstract geometric composition?","value":"Rationalism","group":"Modern Movements","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its development was entangled with the political context of Fascist Italy.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0158","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0158","anchor":"MAJOR:GEOGRAPHY-AND-CIVICS","subject":"What is a city's hinterland?","value":"Its surrounding zone of influence","group":"Map Concepts","major":"Geography & Civics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The relationship may involve trade, services and commuting.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0159","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0159","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes a vault formed by extending an arch along a straight axis?","value":"Barrel vault","group":"Structure","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its continuous curved surface resembles half a cylinder.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0160","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0160","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which prehistoric cave in France is renowned for painted animals discovered in 1940?","value":"Lascaux","group":"Archaeological Discoveries","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its paintings became central to public understanding of Palaeolithic art.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0162","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0162","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes a wall carrying structural loads in addition to its own weight?","value":"Load-bearing wall","group":"Construction","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It differs from a partition that primarily divides interior space.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0164","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0164","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The battles of Marston Moor and Naseby belong to which conflict?","value":"English Civil War","group":"Modern Events","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"They were important victories for parliamentary forces.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0166","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0166","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"At which battle did the Greeks defeat the Persian fleet in narrow waters near Athens?","value":"Salamis","group":"Ancient Battles","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The confined setting limited the advantages of the larger Persian fleet.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0167","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0167","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes a structure whose primary load-bearing elements work mainly in tension?","value":"Tensile structure","group":"Construction","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Membranes and cables are common components.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0168","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0168","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which Persian dynasty made Isfahan a major planned capital under Shah Abbas I?","value":"Safavid dynasty","group":"World Culture","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its monumental square linked palace, commerce and religious architecture.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0169","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0169","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The Este dynasty is particularly associated with which Renaissance state?","value":"Duchy of Ferrara","group":"Italian States","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its court became a centre of literary and artistic patronage.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0171","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0171","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What did the armistice of November 1918 accomplish?","value":"Cessation of fighting with Germany","group":"Worldwar Context","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The formal peace terms were negotiated separately.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0173","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0173","anchor":"MAJOR:LANGUAGE-AND-LITERATURE","subject":"Which opera centres on a hunchbacked court jester and his daughter Gilda?","value":"Rigoletto","group":"Operas","major":"Language & Literature","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The conflict unfolds around power, deception and a father's attempt at revenge.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0174","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0174","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which London housing complex surrounds an arts centre with elevated walkways and concrete towers?","value":"Barbican Estate","group":"European Civic Context","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its planning separates pedestrian routes from much vehicular traffic.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0175","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0175","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Paris building designed as a church by Soufflot became a national mausoleum?","value":"Panthéon","group":"European Civic Context","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its changing role reflects the political history of revolutionary and republican France.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0177","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0177","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which system deliberately compresses concrete before service loads act?","value":"Prestressed concrete","group":"Structural Systems","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The initial compression helps control later tensile stresses and cracking.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0178","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0178","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"What process allows green plants to convert light energy into stored chemical energy?","value":"Photosynthesis","group":"Biology Terms","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Carbon dioxide and water are used to produce organic compounds.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0179","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0179","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"Which instrument measures wind speed?","value":"Anemometer","group":"Scientific Instruments","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Wind data are relevant to climate studies and building design.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0181","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0181","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which term describes a business owned through shares?","value":"joint-stock company","group":"Trade Economics","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Ownership can be distributed among multiple investors.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0182","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0182","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which invention mechanised spinning using multiple spindles operated by one worker?","value":"Spinning jenny","group":"Industrial History","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It was one of several innovations that transformed textile production.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0183","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0183","anchor":"MAJOR:DESIGN","subject":"Which process shapes sheet metal between matching forms under pressure?","value":"Stamping","group":"Metalwork","major":"Design","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It supports repeated manufacture of consistent shapes.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0184","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0184","anchor":"MAJOR:LANGUAGE-AND-LITERATURE","subject":"Which composer wrote the sacred choral work Vespers of 1610?","value":"Claudio Monteverdi","group":"Composers","major":"Language & Literature","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The work stands at the intersection of Renaissance and early Baroque practices.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0185","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0185","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which Spartan king died defending Thermopylae?","value":"Leonidas","group":"Greek People","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The pass became a symbol of resistance to Xerxes' invasion.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0186","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0186","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which movement sought to reduce or eliminate the consumption of alcoholic drink?","value":"Temperance movement","group":"Social Movements","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its campaigns connected moral, social and public-health arguments.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0187","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0187","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"What is a recessed opening in a wall intended to contain a statue called?","value":"Niche","group":"Spatial Terms","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The recess frames and separates the displayed figure.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0188","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0188","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which London railway terminus is associated with Barlow's great single-span train shed?","value":"St Pancras","group":"Industrial Buildings","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The engineering of the shed contrasts with the Gothic Revival hotel façade.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0189","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0189","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"Which Florentine museum preserves telescopes associated with the early observation of Jupiter's moons?","value":"Museo Galileo","group":"Scientific Landmarks","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its collections connect scientific practice with the Medici and Lorraine courts.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0190","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0190","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"What is an enclosed bridge connecting parts of a building above ground level called?","value":"Skybridge","group":"Spatial Terms","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It creates circulation across an intervening gap.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0191","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0191","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"What is the variety of living organisms within an environment called?","value":"Biodiversity","group":"Ecological Terms","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It can be considered at genetic, species and ecosystem levels.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0192","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0192","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes a foundation transferring loads through deep slender elements?","value":"Pile foundation","group":"Construction","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Piles can reach stronger ground or develop resistance along their sides.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0193","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0193","anchor":"MAJOR:GEOGRAPHY-AND-CIVICS","subject":"Which canal crosses Greece's isthmus near the Peloponnese?","value":"Corinth Canal","group":"Waterways","major":"Geography & Civics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its narrow cut links the Gulf of Corinth with the Saronic Gulf.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0194","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0194","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"What does 'patina' refer to on an old building or object?","value":"Surface change acquired over time","group":"Architectural Theory","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It can carry evidence of age, use and environmental exposure.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0195","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0195","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which Dutch city rose as a major seventeenth-century trading and financial centre?","value":"Amsterdam","group":"Mediterranean Trade","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Maritime commerce and financial institutions reinforced its position.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0197","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0197","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Roman construction term describes large squared stone blocks laid in courses?","value":"Opus quadratum","group":"Roman Construction","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The system differs from concrete construction with a thin facing.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0198","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0198","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"What is the division that reduces chromosome number in the production of gametes called?","value":"Meiosis","group":"Biology Terms","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It contributes to genetic variation through recombination and chromosome segregation.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0199","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0199","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes a building or designated space for the rite of baptism?","value":"Baptistery","group":"Church","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"In medieval Italy it was often a separate building.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0200","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0200","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which French cathedral traditionally hosted the coronation of French kings?","value":"Reims Cathedral","group":"Gothic Buildings","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[{"file":"Map record","verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reims_Cathedral","verificationStatus":"inherited_reference_locator_not_retrieved_this_pass","supportScope":"Building context; complete question claim still pending verification"}],"explanation74":"Its political significance accompanied a rich sculptural programme.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0201","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0201","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes a barrier placed in a wall to inhibit the upward movement of moisture?","value":"Damp-proof course","group":"Construction","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It interrupts capillary rise from the ground.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0202","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0202","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which city became the principal capital of the Byzantine Empire?","value":"Constantinople","group":"Medieval Cities","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its position linked Europe and Asia across strategic waterways.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0203","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0203","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes a continuous horizontal band or moulding across a wall?","value":"String course","group":"Facade","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It can mark divisions between storeys or other levels.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0204","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0204","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Porto concert hall by OMA is an irregular faceted volume on a public plaza?","value":"Casa da Música","group":"Contemporary Buildings","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its form encloses a principal auditorium and supporting spaces.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0205","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0205","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"What is the gradual chemical deterioration of a metal through its environment called?","value":"Corrosion","group":"Chemistry Terms","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Rusting of iron is one familiar example.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0206","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0206","anchor":"MAJOR:LANGUAGE-AND-LITERATURE","subject":"Which German silent-film tendency used distorted sets and dramatic shadows?","value":"Expressionist cinema","group":"Cinema Movements","major":"Language & Literature","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Visual design could represent psychological or social disturbance.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0207","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0207","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Neapolitan coastal castle stands on the islet of Megaride?","value":"Castel dell'Ovo","group":"Italian Castles","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its position connects the fortress with the city's ancient harbour setting.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0209","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0209","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"What is a substance composed of two or more chemically bonded elements called?","value":"Compound","group":"Chemistry Terms","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its properties differ from those of a simple physical mixture.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0211","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0211","anchor":"MAJOR:DESIGN","subject":"Which postwar design approach is associated with restrained forms, usability and attention to ordinary domestic life in northern Europe?","value":"Scandinavian modernism","group":"Design Movements","major":"Design","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its objects often balanced industrial production with material warmth.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0213","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0213","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What does source criticism principally assess?","value":"Origin, purpose and reliability","group":"Historical Sources","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"A source's usefulness depends on the question being investigated.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0217","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0217","anchor":"MAJOR:DESIGN","subject":"Which technique joins thin layers of wood with their grain directions alternating?","value":"Plywood construction","group":"Woodwork","major":"Design","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Cross-lamination improves dimensional stability.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0219","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0219","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which city was annexed with its surrounding territory after the plebiscite of 1866 in Venetia?","value":"Venice","group":"Italian Context","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The transfer followed the Austro-Prussian conflict and Italian participation.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0220","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0220","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which organisation developed the conventions protecting people affected by armed conflict?","value":"International Committee of the Red Cross","group":"Modern Institutions","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It has a distinctive humanitarian role under the Geneva Conventions.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0221","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0221","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What is oral history principally based on?","value":"Recorded personal testimony","group":"Historical Sources","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Memory provides evidence that must be contextualised critically.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0222","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0222","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes a continuous colonnade surrounding a building or courtyard?","value":"Peristyle","group":"Classical","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"A peristyle creates a columned boundary around an interior or exterior space.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0223","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0223","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Amsterdam exchange building by Berlage is recognised for its massive brick forms?","value":"Beurs van Berlage","group":"European Civic Context","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its construction and spatial clarity influenced later Dutch architecture.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0224","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0224","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"Which SI unit measures electrical resistance?","value":"Ohm","group":"Measurement","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Resistance relates voltage to current in Ohm's law.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0226","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0226","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes the principal longitudinal space of a church used by the congregation?","value":"Nave","group":"Church","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It is often flanked by aisles.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0227","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0227","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which Italian town became the name of an early Iron Age culture after cemetery discoveries nearby?","value":"Villanova","group":"Archaeological Discoveries","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The term is used for material culture associated with early Etruscan development.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0228","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0228","anchor":"MAJOR:LANGUAGE-AND-LITERATURE","subject":"Which Italian epic narrates a Christian army's struggle to recover Jerusalem?","value":"Jerusalem Delivered","group":"Italian Texts","major":"Language & Literature","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Tasso adapts the First Crusade into a religious and heroic poem.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0229","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0229","anchor":"MAJOR:DESIGN","subject":"Which process refines details on the front of a metal surface with tools?","value":"Chasing","group":"Metalwork","major":"Design","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It often accompanies repoussé work.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0231","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0231","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Roman church contains the Chapel of Saint Zeno with ninth-century mosaics?","value":"Santa Prassede","group":"Church Features","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its decoration belongs to the artistic patronage of Pope Paschal I.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0232","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0232","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which thinker defended a strong sovereign in Leviathan?","value":"Thomas Hobbes","group":"Political Thought","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"His argument begins from the dangers of conflict without common authority.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0233","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0233","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Sydney performing-arts complex uses groups of shell-like roof forms?","value":"Sydney Opera House","group":"Contemporary Buildings","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The roofs create a distinctive profile beside the harbour.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0235","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0235","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes a substantial vertical masonry support?","value":"Pier","group":"Structure","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Piers may support arches, vaults or bridges.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0236","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0236","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which Iberian city was the centre of an Umayyad caliphate?","value":"Córdoba","group":"Medieval Cities","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its court and institutions supported a major cultural flowering.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0238","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0238","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Who led the forces that recaptured Jerusalem from the Crusaders in 1187?","value":"Saladin","group":"Medieval People","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"His victory at Hattin preceded the city's recovery.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0239","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0239","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"At which siege did Caesar trap Vercingetorix while also resisting a relief army?","value":"Alesia","group":"Ancient Battles","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The siege was decisive in the Roman conquest of Gaul.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0240","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0240","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which site did excavations beginning in the eighteenth century help make central to European neoclassical taste?","value":"Pompeii","group":"Archaeological Discoveries","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its domestic decoration and urban remains offered new evidence of ancient life.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0241","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0241","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Tuscan cathedral stands beside a detached baptistery and famously leaning campanile?","value":"Pisa Cathedral","group":"Church Features","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[{"file":"Map record","verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pisa_Cathedral","verificationStatus":"inherited_reference_locator_not_retrieved_this_pass","supportScope":"Building context; complete question claim still pending verification"}],"explanation74":"The monuments form an ensemble in the Piazza dei Miracoli.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0242","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0242","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"What is the division that normally produces two genetically similar body cells called?","value":"Mitosis","group":"Biology Terms","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It supports growth and tissue maintenance.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0243","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0243","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which First World War offensive is associated with enormous British losses on its first day?","value":"Somme","group":"Modern Battles","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The prolonged campaign exemplified the costs of trench warfare.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0244","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0244","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Acropolis building incorporated several cult sites and a porch of female sculptural supports?","value":"Erechtheion","group":"Ancient Buildings","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its irregular arrangement responded to multiple sacred associations.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0245","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0245","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes a bell tower, often standing apart from a church?","value":"Campanile","group":"Church","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The term is especially associated with Italian examples.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0246","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0246","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Roman concrete component helped some mortars set in wet conditions?","value":"Pozzolanic volcanic ash","group":"Roman Construction","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its reaction with lime contributed to hydraulic properties.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0248","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0248","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes a vertical member dividing a window into separate lights?","value":"Mullion","group":"Facade","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"A horizontal dividing member is a transom.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0249","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0249","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The Battle of Sedan led to the fall of Napoleon III during which conflict?","value":"Franco-Prussian War","group":"Modern Events","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"His capture helped bring the Second Empire to an end.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0251","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0251","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"Which instrument records ground motion during earthquakes?","value":"Seismograph","group":"Scientific Instruments","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its record can be used to analyse seismic waves.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0252","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0252","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which reformer is associated with Geneva and the doctrine of predestination?","value":"John Calvin","group":"Earlymodern People","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Geneva became an influential centre of Reformed Protestantism.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0253","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0253","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which drawing places a building within its plot and surroundings?","value":"Site plan","group":"Architectural Drawing","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It can show access, orientation, boundaries and landscape.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0254","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0254","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Tuscan town is particularly associated with a surviving skyline of medieval family towers?","value":"San Gimignano","group":"Italian Urban History","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The towers reflect competition and status within the medieval town.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0256","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0256","anchor":"MAJOR:LANGUAGE-AND-LITERATURE","subject":"Which composer wrote the orchestral work La mer?","value":"Claude Debussy","group":"Composers","major":"Language & Literature","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its treatment of colour and movement avoids literal musical illustration.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0257","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0257","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Bologna building originally gathered the university's teaching spaces and contains an anatomical theatre?","value":"Archiginnasio","group":"Italian Civic Buildings","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its architecture records the institutional life of the historic university.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0259","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0259","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"A building organised around a dominant central space has which plan type?","value":"Central plan","group":"Plan Types","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Circular, polygonal and other symmetrical forms can support it.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0260","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0260","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which European state ruled Indonesia as the Dutch East Indies?","value":"Netherlands","group":"Colonial Powers","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The colonial economy developed through trade and territorial administration.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0261","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0261","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which roof slopes on all four sides of a rectangular building?","value":"Hip roof","group":"Roof Forms","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It has no full vertical gable at its ends.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0262","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0262","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The Achaemenid Empire was centred on which people?","value":"Persians","group":"Ancient States","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its territories extended from the Near East into Egypt and parts of Asia.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0263","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0263","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which Mesopotamian city is associated with a royal cemetery excavated by Leonard Woolley?","value":"Ur","group":"Archaeological Discoveries","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The finds provided evidence of elite burial and craftsmanship.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0265","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0265","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which Persian ruler reorganised imperial government into satrapies?","value":"Darius I","group":"Ancient Rulers","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Satraps governed provinces within the imperial administration.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0266","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0266","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What was the Great Western Schism?","value":"A division among rival papal claimants","group":"Medieval Terms","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It should not be confused with the split between eastern and western churches.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0267","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0267","anchor":"MAJOR:LANGUAGE-AND-LITERATURE","subject":"Which Italian conductor directed La Scala and later the NBC Symphony Orchestra?","value":"Arturo Toscanini","group":"Cultural Figures","major":"Language & Literature","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"His career linked Italian and American musical institutions.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0268","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0268","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which civilisation developed monumental cities such as Tikal and a complex calendar system?","value":"Maya","group":"World Culture","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its cultural history extended across parts of Mesoamerica.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0270","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0270","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which movement promoted traditional street networks and walkable mixed-use neighbourhoods in reaction to sprawl?","value":"New Urbanism","group":"Urban Models","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its projects draw on selected patterns of older towns.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0271","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0271","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What was the mandate system after the First World War?","value":"Administration of former imperial territories","group":"Worldwar Context","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It placed territories under powers supervised nominally by the League of Nations.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0274","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0274","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which battle is known as Napoleon's victory over the Austrian and Russian emperors?","value":"Austerlitz","group":"Napoleonic Battles","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The victory reshaped central European politics.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0275","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0275","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes a horizontal member connecting supports to restrain their spreading?","value":"Tie beam","group":"Structure","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"In a roof truss it can resist outward thrust.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0276","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0276","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Venetian basilica uses a five-domed Greek-cross arrangement?","value":"Saint Mark's Basilica","group":"Church Features","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[{"file":"Map record","verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St_Mark%27s_Basilica","verificationStatus":"inherited_reference_locator_not_retrieved_this_pass","supportScope":"Building context; complete question claim still pending verification"}],"explanation74":"The form reflects strong connections with Byzantine architectural traditions.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0277","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0277","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"What is a 'grotto' in a designed garden?","value":"An artificial cave-like feature","group":"Landscape Forms","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It can combine water, rockwork and mythological associations.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0278","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0278","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What was a principal effect of the Irish Great Famine?","value":"Mass death and emigration","group":"Nineteenth Context","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Potato blight interacted with poverty and political-economic conditions.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0280","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0280","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The siege of Sevastopol in the 1850s was a major episode of which conflict?","value":"Crimean War","group":"Modern Events","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The war involved Russia against an alliance including Britain and France.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0281","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0281","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Roman power plant became a museum combining machinery with ancient sculpture?","value":"Centrale Montemartini","group":"Architecture Adaptation","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The display creates a deliberate encounter between industrial and classical heritage.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0283","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0283","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"What is a projecting upper floor extending beyond the wall below called in timber buildings?","value":"Jetty","group":"Spatial Terms","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The projection increases upper-floor area and shapes the street frontage.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0284","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0284","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"Who demonstrated that microorganisms contribute to fermentation and developed a heat-treatment process?","value":"Louis Pasteur","group":"Scientific People","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"His research connected microbiology with practical control of spoilage and disease.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0285","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0285","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which French politician proposed pooling French and German coal and steel production?","value":"Robert Schuman","group":"Ww2 People","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The proposal became a foundational step in European integration.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0286","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0286","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which papal encyclical of 1891 addressed the condition of workers?","value":"Rerum Novarum","group":"Historical Documents","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It became foundational for modern Catholic social teaching.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0287","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0287","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The Avignon Papacy refers to which situation?","value":"Papal residence outside Rome","group":"Religious History","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Several fourteenth-century popes resided in Avignon.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0289","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0289","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes an ornamental feature marking the top of a pinnacle, gable or similar element?","value":"Finial","group":"Church","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Finials crown and emphasize architectural points.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0290","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0290","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The Battle of Lepanto occurred within which broader struggle?","value":"Ottoman–Venetian War","group":"Modern Events","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The Holy League's naval victory did not reverse all Ottoman territorial gains.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0292","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0292","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which US constitutional text begins with 'We the People'?","value":"Constitution of the United States","group":"Historical Documents","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It established the framework of the federal government.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0293","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0293","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes a vertical structural element designed to resist lateral forces in its plane?","value":"Shear wall","group":"Construction","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It helps stabilize buildings against wind and earthquakes.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0294","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0294","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes a projecting roof-water spout, often carved as a creature?","value":"Gargoyle","group":"Church","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its practical function distinguishes it from purely decorative grotesques.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0295","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0295","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Italian architect and theorist connected conservation of monuments with their urban surroundings?","value":"Gustavo Giovannoni","group":"Restoration People","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"His work addressed both individual buildings and historic urban fabric.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0296","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0296","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Vicentine civic building received Palladio's loggias with repeated Serlian openings?","value":"Basilica Palladiana","group":"Renaissance Buildings","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The new envelope adapted an existing municipal complex.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0297","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0297","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes a spiral scroll characteristic of an Ionic capital?","value":"Volute","group":"Classical","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Paired scrolls distinguish the Ionic capital.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0298","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0298","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What is historiography?","value":"The study of historical writing","group":"Historical Sources","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It examines how interpretations and methods change.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0300","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0300","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes an upper-storey bay window projecting from a wall without reaching the ground?","value":"Oriel","group":"Facade","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It is generally supported by brackets or corbels.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0301","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0301","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which nineteenth-century invention enabled recorded sound to be played back?","value":"Phonograph","group":"Industrial History","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its recording principle preceded later disc-based systems.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0302","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0302","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The office of doge is strongly associated with which maritime republic?","value":"Republic of Venice","group":"Italian States","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The doge operated within a complex oligarchic political system.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0303","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0303","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What was a Roman 'triumph'?","value":"A victory procession","group":"Ancient Terms","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It publicly honoured a successful military commander.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0305","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0305","anchor":"MAJOR:GEOGRAPHY-AND-CIVICS","subject":"Which canal connects the North Sea and the Baltic through northern Germany?","value":"Kiel Canal","group":"Waterways","major":"Geography & Civics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It shortens the route around the Danish peninsula.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0306","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0306","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which ancient Anatolian city contained the Library of Celsus?","value":"Ephesus","group":"Ancient Sites","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The library's monumental façade expressed civic and commemorative ambitions.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0308","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0308","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes an external device that shades a building from direct sunlight?","value":"Brise-soleil","group":"Facade","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It reduces solar gain while allowing daylight and views.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0309","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0309","anchor":"MAJOR:DESIGN","subject":"Which process joins metals with a lower-melting filler without melting the main pieces?","value":"Soldering","group":"Metalwork","major":"Design","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The filler bonds the surfaces at the joint.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0311","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0311","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Who founded the philosophical school known as the Garden?","value":"Epicurus","group":"Greek People","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The school linked philosophy to tranquillity and freedom from fear.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0312","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0312","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Japanese movement imagined expandable urban structures and replaceable building units?","value":"Metabolism","group":"Modern Movements","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Biological metaphors informed proposals for growth and transformation.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0313","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0313","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which ruler is associated with the library excavated at Nineveh?","value":"Ashurbanipal","group":"Ancient Rulers","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The library preserved thousands of cuneiform tablets.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0314","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0314","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes an ornament placed at the apex or corner of a pediment?","value":"Acroterion","group":"Classical","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It is positioned on the exterior outline of the temple roof.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0315","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0315","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which ornament resembles a continuous wave or running scroll?","value":"Vitruvian scroll","group":"Architectural Ornament","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its repeated curved motif appears in classical decorative vocabularies.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0316","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0316","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which settlement restored peace after the Franco-Prussian War?","value":"Treaty of Frankfurt","group":"Treaties","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"France ceded Alsace and part of Lorraine to the new German Empire.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0317","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0317","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What did Lorenzo Valla challenge by analysing the language of the Donation of Constantine?","value":"The document's authenticity","group":"Intellectual Context","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its vocabulary and usage were inconsistent with the claimed ancient origin.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0318","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0318","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which Roman leader defeated Antony and Cleopatra at Actium?","value":"Octavian","group":"Roman People","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The victory enabled him to consolidate power before becoming Augustus.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0319","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0319","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes the projecting support or course from which an arch springs?","value":"Impost","group":"Structure","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It defines the transition into the arch.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0320","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0320","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Renaissance decorative mode combines delicate fantastical figures, plants and architectural motifs?","value":"Grotesque ornament","group":"Architectural Ornament","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its name derives from the rediscovery of ancient painted rooms treated as grottoes.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0321","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0321","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What were 'satraps' in the Persian Empire?","value":"Provincial governors","group":"Ancient Terms","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"They administered territories under the authority of the king.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0322","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0322","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which roof has two sloping planes meeting at a ridge?","value":"Gable roof","group":"Roof Forms","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The ends form gables unless altered by another roof form.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0323","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0323","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"Which energy source exploits the regular rise and fall of sea level?","value":"Tidal energy","group":"Energy Sources","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The underlying motion is strongly influenced by gravitational interactions.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0324","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0324","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"What is the conversion of sound energy into other forms within a material called?","value":"Absorption","group":"Light Sound","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Absorptive surfaces help control room acoustics.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0325","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0325","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The battles of Valmy and Jemappes belong to which conflict?","value":"French Revolutionary Wars","group":"Modern Events","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"They occurred during the early military defence and expansion of revolutionary France.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0326","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0326","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which battle ended with Richard III's death and Henry Tudor's victory?","value":"Bosworth Field","group":"Medieval Battles","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The victory established the Tudor monarchy.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0327","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0327","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Oslo cultural building allows visitors to walk over its sloping roof?","value":"Oslo Opera House","group":"Contemporary Buildings","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The roof extends public space into the building's form.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0328","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0328","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Barcelona hospital complex by Domènech i Montaner uses landscaped pavilions and rich ornament?","value":"Hospital de Sant Pau","group":"European Civic Context","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The plan combined medical organisation with environmental and artistic concerns.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0330","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0330","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What characterised much Italian internal migration during the postwar boom?","value":"Movement from the south to northern industrial cities","group":"Italian Social History","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The process reshaped urban housing and social life.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0331","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0331","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which late Roman building in the Forum used enormous cross-vaulted bays?","value":"Basilica of Maxentius","group":"Ancient Buildings","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its scale and structure influenced later monumental architecture.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0332","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0332","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What did Renaissance philology seek to establish through comparison of manuscripts?","value":"Accurate texts and meanings","group":"Intellectual Context","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Language and historical context helped identify errors and later alterations.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0333","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0333","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which archaeological site preserves a Roman city buried along with Pompeii but by different volcanic deposits?","value":"Herculaneum","group":"Ancient Sites","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The burial conditions preserved organic materials in exceptional cases.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0334","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0334","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes the vertical wall or cylindrical base beneath a dome?","value":"Drum","group":"Structure","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It can raise the dome and accommodate windows.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0335","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0335","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"What term describes an organism's genetic constitution?","value":"Genotype","group":"Biology Terms","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It is distinct from the traits that are visibly expressed.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0336","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0336","anchor":"MAJOR:DESIGN","subject":"Which finishing method builds up thin layers of shellac using a pad?","value":"French polishing","group":"Woodwork","major":"Design","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The process can create a deep glossy surface.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0337","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0337","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which European state controlled the Congo as a colony after Leopold II's personal regime ended?","value":"Belgium","group":"Colonial Powers","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The transfer did not end coercive colonial exploitation.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0338","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0338","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which sedimentary stone consists mainly of consolidated sand-sized grains?","value":"Sandstone","group":"Stone Materials","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its colour and durability depend on grains and cementing material.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0339","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0339","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"Which London institution opened in 1759 with collections including those of Hans Sloane?","value":"British Museum","group":"Scientific Landmarks","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its early collections included natural history as well as antiquities.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0340","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0340","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which London power station was converted into Tate Modern?","value":"Bankside Power Station","group":"Architecture Adaptation","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The conversion retained the monumental turbine hall as a central space.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0341","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0341","anchor":"MAJOR:DESIGN","subject":"What is a full-scale preliminary version used to test a design called?","value":"Prototype","group":"Design Terms","major":"Design","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Testing can reveal problems before production begins.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0342","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0342","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which paired battles shattered Prussian forces in 1806?","value":"Jena and Auerstedt","group":"Napoleonic Battles","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The defeats exposed weaknesses in the Prussian military system.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0343","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0343","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Italian group included the young Rationalists who issued manifestos in the 1920s?","value":"Gruppo 7","group":"Architecture Groups","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"They sought a modern architecture while discussing continuity with tradition.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0346","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0346","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"What is the separation of white light into its component colours called?","value":"Dispersion","group":"Light Sound","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Different wavelengths are refracted by different amounts.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0347","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0347","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which term describes borrowing owed by the state?","value":"public debt","group":"Trade Economics","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It differs from the debts of private households or firms.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0349","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0349","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Who founded the Achaemenid Persian Empire?","value":"Cyrus II","group":"Ancient Rulers","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"His conquests united Persian power across a large Near Eastern empire.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0351","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0351","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes a roofed space open on one or more sides through arches or columns?","value":"Loggia","group":"Facade","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It connects interior and exterior environments.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0352","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0352","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which medieval route network connected Mediterranean markets with silk-producing regions of Asia?","value":"Silk Roads","group":"Mediterranean Trade","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The term covers multiple changing overland and maritime routes.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0353","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0353","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes the rounded moulding beneath the abacus of a Doric capital?","value":"Echinus","group":"Classical","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its profile varies across periods and examples.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0354","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0354","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Milanese fortress became a major ducal residence under the Sforza?","value":"Castello Sforzesco","group":"Italian Castles","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its successive uses include military, residential and museum functions.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0355","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0355","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which Italian maritime city developed major holdings including Crete and Cyprus?","value":"Venice","group":"Mediterranean Trade","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its overseas territories supported commercial and strategic interests.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0356","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0356","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"What is the plane of Earth's orbit projected onto the sky called?","value":"Ecliptic","group":"Astronomy Terms","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The Sun appears to move along it over the year.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0357","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0357","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"Which instrument measures angles in surveying?","value":"Theodolite","group":"Scientific Instruments","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Angular measurements help establish positions and alignments.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0358","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0358","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which French leader appealed from London for continued resistance in June 1940?","value":"Charles de Gaulle","group":"Ww2 People","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The appeal became a founding episode of Free France.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0359","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0359","anchor":"MAJOR:GEOGRAPHY-AND-CIVICS","subject":"What do contour lines on a topographic map connect?","value":"Points of equal elevation","group":"Map Concepts","major":"Geography & Civics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Their spacing indicates the steepness of the terrain.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0360","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0360","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which ancient civilisation developed in Anatolia with Hattusa as its capital?","value":"Hittites","group":"Ancient States","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Hittite power interacted with Egypt and other Near Eastern kingdoms.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0361","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0361","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What happened to the western imperial office after the deposition of Romulus Augustulus?","value":"It ceased to have a separate western emperor","group":"Roman Changes","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Roman institutions and the eastern empire continued.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0362","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0362","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which association was founded in Germany to improve the relationship between design and industrial production?","value":"Deutscher Werkbund","group":"Architecture Groups","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its debates concerned quality, standardisation and artistic individuality.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0363","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0363","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which Indian independence leader promoted non-violent civil disobedience?","value":"Mahatma Gandhi","group":"Ww2 People","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"His campaigns linked mass mobilisation with resistance to colonial rule.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0364","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0364","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"Which Greenwich institution became associated with the reference meridian for longitude?","value":"Royal Observatory","group":"Scientific Landmarks","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The prime meridian became a standard for geographical coordinates.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0366","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0366","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which arch is constructed by progressively projecting horizontal masonry courses rather than true voussoirs?","value":"Corbel arch","group":"Arch Types","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It does not operate as a true compression arch with radial joints.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0367","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0367","anchor":"MAJOR:DESIGN","subject":"Which technique bends steamed solid wood around a form?","value":"Steam bending","group":"Woodwork","major":"Design","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Moisture and heat temporarily increase the wood's flexibility.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0368","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0368","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"At which battle did Caesar defeat Pompey's principal army in Greece?","value":"Pharsalus","group":"Ancient Battles","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Pompey fled to Egypt after the defeat.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0369","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0369","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"What is a lasting change in genetic material called?","value":"Mutation","group":"Biology Terms","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its effects can be harmful, neutral or beneficial depending on context.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0370","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0370","anchor":"MAJOR:DESIGN","subject":"What is the spacing between particular pairs of letters called?","value":"Kerning","group":"Graphic Design","major":"Design","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It corrects visually awkward gaps between letter shapes.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0371","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0371","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which ancient people are particularly associated with Tyre and maritime trading colonies?","value":"Phoenicians","group":"Ancient States","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Their Mediterranean networks included the settlement of Carthage.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0372","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0372","anchor":"MAJOR:GEOGRAPHY-AND-CIVICS","subject":"What is a ring-shaped coral reef enclosing a lagoon called?","value":"Atoll","group":"Landforms","major":"Geography & Civics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its development is often associated with a subsiding volcanic island.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0373","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0373","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"What is a 'pergola'?","value":"A framework supporting climbing plants","group":"Landscape Forms","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It creates a shaded route or sitting area.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0374","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0374","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"What does the architectural term 'tectonic' chiefly concern?","value":"Construction and its expression","group":"Architectural Theory","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It links the act of building with the visible articulation of materials and joints.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0376","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0376","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which term describes specialisation into separate tasks?","value":"division of labour","group":"Trade Economics","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It can raise productivity while changing skills and working conditions.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0377","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0377","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Venetian commercial interior by Carlo Scarpa was designed for a typewriter manufacturer?","value":"Olivetti Showroom in Piazza San Marco","group":"Modern Italian Context","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Materials, levels and display details transform a narrow urban interior.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0378","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0378","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which family supported the literary court associated with Ariosto in Ferrara?","value":"Este","group":"Renaissance Patronage","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Court patronage connected literature with dynastic representation.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0379","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0379","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What was the Delian League originally formed to coordinate?","value":"Resistance to Persia","group":"Ancient Terms","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The alliance later became an instrument of Athenian power.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0380","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0380","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which ruler established a Greek-speaking dynasty in Egypt after Alexander's death?","value":"Ptolemy I","group":"Ancient Rulers","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The Ptolemaic kingdom made Alexandria a major cultural centre.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0381","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0381","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What were the mendicant orders particularly associated with?","value":"Preaching and voluntary poverty","group":"Medieval Terms","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Franciscans and Dominicans developed important urban roles.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0382","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0382","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Rome museum by Zaha Hadid uses intersecting gallery routes and flowing concrete forms?","value":"MAXXI","group":"Contemporary Buildings","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The design treats circulation as a central organising element.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0383","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0383","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which Roman politician exposed the conspiracy of Catiline?","value":"Cicero","group":"Roman People","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"His speeches against Catiline became major works of Latin political rhetoric.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0385","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0385","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"What is excessive nutrient enrichment of water commonly called?","value":"Eutrophication","group":"Ecological Terms","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It can lead to algal growth and depletion of dissolved oxygen.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0386","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0386","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which villa near Pompeii gives its name to a celebrated room of large painted figures?","value":"Villa of the Mysteries","group":"Italian Villas","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The exact interpretation of the painted ritual scene remains debated.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0387","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0387","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"Which metal is the principal constituent of steel?","value":"Iron","group":"Materials Science","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Carbon and other alloying elements modify its properties.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0388","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0388","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which roof has repeated asymmetrical ridges often used to admit industrial daylight?","value":"Sawtooth roof","group":"Roof Forms","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The glazed faces can be oriented to control direct sunlight.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0390","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0390","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What was the Algerian FLN?","value":"An independence movement","group":"Postcolonial Context","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It fought French colonial rule and later dominated the new state.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0391","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0391","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes an elongated covered colonnade in ancient Greek public architecture?","value":"Stoa","group":"Urban","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It sheltered activities along agoras and other civic spaces.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0392","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0392","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What was the central issue in the Dreyfus Affair?","value":"The wrongful conviction of a French officer","group":"Nineteenth Context","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The case exposed antisemitism and conflict over the army and republic.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0393","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0393","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The Albigensian Crusade was directed principally against which religious group?","value":"Cathars","group":"Religious History","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The conflict also strengthened northern French power in the south.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0394","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0394","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which term describes farming mainly for direct consumption?","value":"subsistence agriculture","group":"Trade Economics","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Only a limited surplus may be available for markets.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0395","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0395","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which battle was a major Swedish victory under Gustavus Adolphus in the Thirty Years' War?","value":"Breitenfeld","group":"Earlymodern Battles","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The victory strengthened the Protestant military position.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0396","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0396","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which British writer argued strongly against destructive restoration in The Seven Lamps of Architecture?","value":"John Ruskin","group":"Restoration People","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"He valued age and the historical evidence carried by buildings.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0397","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0397","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which structure uses an interlocking three-dimensional network of linear members?","value":"Space frame","group":"Structural Systems","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The network can span large areas with relatively light components.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0399","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0399","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The Italian military defeat of 1896 occurred near which Ethiopian city?","value":"Adwa","group":"Italian Context","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The victory preserved Ethiopian independence against Italian invasion.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0400","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0400","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes a moulded or decorated band following the curve of an arch?","value":"Archivolt","group":"Church","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Successive archivolts often frame medieval church portals.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0401","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0401","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What was a principal effect of the Sack of Rome in 1527 on artistic networks?","value":"Dispersal of artists and patrons","group":"Renaissance Context","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The disruption helped spread artistic practices beyond Rome.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0402","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0402","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"Which fuel is formed mainly from ancient plant matter under heat and pressure?","value":"Coal","group":"Energy Sources","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It is a fossil fuel rather than a resource renewed on human timescales.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0403","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0403","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"At Paimio Sanatorium, the long balconies were designed chiefly for:","value":"Patients’ exposure to fresh air","group":"Modern Buildings","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The terraces formed part of the tuberculosis-care programme before modern antibiotic treatment.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0404","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0404","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which naval battle destroyed much of the French fleet supporting Napoleon's Egyptian expedition?","value":"Battle of the Nile","group":"Napoleonic Battles","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The loss isolated the French army in Egypt.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0405","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0405","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which German cathedral was completed in the nineteenth century following its medieval Gothic design?","value":"Cologne Cathedral","group":"Gothic Buildings","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[{"file":"Map record","verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cologne_Cathedral","verificationStatus":"inherited_reference_locator_not_retrieved_this_pass","supportScope":"Building context; complete question claim still pending verification"}],"explanation74":"Its long construction history illustrates later revival of medieval intentions.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0406","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0406","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Naples castle is also known as Maschio Angioino?","value":"Castel Nuovo","group":"Italian Castles","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its later triumphal entrance combines royal representation with a fortified complex.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0407","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0407","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which drawing represents a building as cut by a horizontal plane?","value":"Plan","group":"Architectural Drawing","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It reveals spatial arrangement at a selected height.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0408","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0408","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"What is a homogeneous mixture in which one substance is dispersed at the molecular or ionic level called?","value":"Solution","group":"Chemistry Terms","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The dissolved substance is distributed throughout the solvent.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0409","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0409","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which arch has a curve forming half a circle?","value":"Semicircular arch","group":"Arch Types","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It is prominent in Roman and Romanesque architecture.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0410","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0410","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which Spanish cave became famous for its prehistoric painted bison?","value":"Altamira","group":"Archaeological Discoveries","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The recognition of its antiquity changed views of early art.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0411","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0411","anchor":"MAJOR:GEOGRAPHY-AND-CIVICS","subject":"What is a tidal, partly enclosed river mouth with mixed fresh and salt water called?","value":"Estuary","group":"Landforms","major":"Geography & Civics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its character depends on river flow, tides and coastal form.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0412","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0412","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What did the scientific revolution encourage in studying nature?","value":"Observation and mathematical explanation","group":"Intellectual Context","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its development was uneven and involved both continuity and change.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0413","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0413","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Who led Athens during much of its fifth-century cultural flourishing?","value":"Pericles","group":"Greek People","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The rebuilding of the Acropolis formed part of this political and cultural setting.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0414","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0414","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Bologna square is bordered by San Petronio and major civic palaces?","value":"Piazza Maggiore","group":"Urban Spaces","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Religious and communal institutions share the central public space.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0415","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0415","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which ancient city near modern Hisarlık was investigated by Schliemann in connection with Homer?","value":"Troy","group":"Archaeological Discoveries","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The site contains many settlement layers from different periods.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0416","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0416","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What is 'non-alignment' in postcolonial diplomacy?","value":"Independence from rival military blocs","group":"Historical Concepts","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It did not necessarily mean neutrality on every international issue.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0417","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0417","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"What is a 'belvedere' primarily intended to provide?","value":"A commanding view","group":"Landscape Forms","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It may be a terrace, pavilion or elevated room.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0419","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0419","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which system supports floors through a framework of columns and beams rather than exterior masonry walls?","value":"Skeleton frame","group":"Structural Systems","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The enclosing façade need not carry the floors above.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0420","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0420","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What did the recovery of Greek manuscripts contribute to Renaissance culture?","value":"Renewed access to ancient texts","group":"Renaissance Context","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Translation and philological study broadened classical learning.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0421","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0421","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"What does 'genius loci' refer to in architectural discussion?","value":"The character of a place","group":"Architectural Theory","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The concept connects design with the qualities of a particular setting.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0422","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0422","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What did the Vajont disaster demonstrate in relation to infrastructure?","value":"The consequences of geological instability","group":"Italian Social History","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"A landslide displaced reservoir water and devastated settlements below.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0423","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0423","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes masonry treatment emphasizing the joints or rough-faced blocks?","value":"Rustication","group":"Facade","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It is often used to give a lower storey a robust visual character.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0425","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0425","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which volcanic stone is formed from consolidated ash and is common in central Italian construction?","value":"Tuff","group":"Stone Materials","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its properties vary according to the volcanic material and degree of consolidation.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0426","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0426","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which building type housed a community of monks around shared religious and domestic spaces?","value":"Monastery","group":"Historic Types","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Church, cloister and service buildings formed a connected complex.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0427","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0427","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What linked Manila and Acapulco in the Spanish imperial system?","value":"A trans-Pacific trading route","group":"Exploration","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The galleons connected Asian goods with American silver.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0428","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0428","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which king's victories against Rome gave rise to the expression 'Pyrrhic victory'?","value":"Pyrrhus","group":"Ancient Rulers","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"His successes imposed losses that were difficult to replace.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0429","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0429","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What was the central aim of the US civil rights movement?","value":"Ending racial discrimination","group":"Postcolonial Context","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Campaigns targeted segregation and restrictions on voting.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0430","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0430","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which castle near Turin was converted into a museum of contemporary art?","value":"Castello di Rivoli","group":"Italian Castles","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The museum reuses an unfinished Savoy residence.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0431","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0431","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which English dynasty included Henry II and Richard I?","value":"Plantagenets","group":"Medieval Dynasties","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its territories and claims linked England closely with France.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0432","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0432","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which church in Palermo forms part of the Norman royal palace and combines mosaics with a painted wooden ceiling?","value":"Palatine Chapel","group":"Church Features","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its decoration demonstrates the multicultural character of Norman Sicily.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0433","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0433","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which roof construction uses cables and a tensioned membrane rather than a conventional rigid covering?","value":"Tensile membrane roof","group":"Roof Forms","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its stability depends on geometry, pretension and supports.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0434","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0434","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Sicilian city was rebuilt on a new site after the earthquake of 1693?","value":"Noto","group":"Italian Urban History","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its reconstruction produced a coordinated Baroque urban ensemble.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0435","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0435","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What did antiquarian scholarship principally examine?","value":"Material and textual remains of the past","group":"Intellectual Context","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its collecting and documentation contributed to archaeology and art history.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0437","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0437","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"Which mode of heat transfer involves the bulk motion of a fluid?","value":"Convection","group":"Building Physics","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Warm and cool air currents are familiar examples.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0438","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0438","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which civilisation used Linear B to write an early form of Greek?","value":"Mycenaean civilisation","group":"Ancient States","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The script differs from the still undeciphered Linear A.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0439","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0439","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes the temporary mould supporting fresh concrete until it gains sufficient strength?","value":"Formwork","group":"Construction","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its shape determines the cast concrete surface and geometry.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0440","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0440","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Berlin museum by Mies uses a broad steel roof over a largely open glass hall?","value":"Neue Nationalgalerie","group":"Modern Buildings","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The main hall exemplifies his interest in flexible universal space.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0441","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0441","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Who made Nineveh a principal Assyrian royal centre?","value":"Sennacherib","group":"Ancient Rulers","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"His building programme transformed the Assyrian capital.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0443","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0443","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which pre-unification state was governed directly by the pope?","value":"Papal States","group":"Italian States","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its territories extended beyond Rome into central Italy.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0444","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0444","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which European state controlled Namibia as German South West Africa?","value":"Germany","group":"Colonial Powers","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its colonial rule included genocide against the Herero and Nama.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0445","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0445","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which Urbino dynasty is associated with Federico's ducal palace and humanist library?","value":"Montefeltro","group":"Renaissance Patronage","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The court cultivated an image of military authority and learning.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0446","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0446","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What was the Schlieffen Plan intended to avoid?","value":"A prolonged war on two fronts","group":"Worldwar Context","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its strategy depended on a rapid defeat of France before turning east.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0447","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0447","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What did civic pageants and triumphal entries communicate in Renaissance cities?","value":"Public representations of political authority","group":"Renaissance Context","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Temporary architecture and spectacle made power visible.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0448","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0448","anchor":"MAJOR:DESIGN","subject":"Which process shapes metal by hammering or pressing rather than pouring it into a mould?","value":"Forging","group":"Metalwork","major":"Design","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It changes the form of solid metal through force.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0449","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0449","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which New York elevated freight railway became a public linear park?","value":"High Line","group":"Architecture Adaptation","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The project reused infrastructure for pedestrian and landscape space.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0450","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0450","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes a shallow rectangular vertical projection articulated like a column?","value":"Pilaster","group":"Facade","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It may have a base and capital while remaining attached to a wall.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0451","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0451","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes a courtyard bordered by covered walks in a religious complex?","value":"Cloister","group":"Church","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It organizes circulation and provides a sheltered communal space.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0452","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0452","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes a Roman dining room associated with reclining couches?","value":"Triclinium","group":"Urban","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its name reflects the conventional arrangement of three couches.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0453","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0453","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which technology enabled rapid written communication through electrical signals?","value":"Electric telegraph","group":"Industrial History","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It transformed communication over long distances before the telephone.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0454","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0454","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"A settlement whose main routes extend from a central point has which plan type?","value":"Radial plan","group":"Plan Types","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The geometry emphasises a central focus.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0455","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0455","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What is 'protectionism'?","value":"Restriction of foreign competition","group":"Historical Concepts","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Tariffs and import limits are common instruments.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0456","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0456","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which Portuguese prince sponsored Atlantic exploration and is known as 'the Navigator'?","value":"Henry the Navigator","group":"Earlymodern People","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"His patronage supported Portuguese maritime expansion.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0457","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0457","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which term describes coordination among competing producers?","value":"cartel","group":"Trade Economics","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Members may agree on output or prices while remaining separate firms.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0458","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0458","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What did the Republic of Letters describe in early modern Europe?","value":"A network of learned exchange","group":"Intellectual Context","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Correspondence and publications connected scholars across political borders.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0460","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0460","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Ottoman building type served as a public bath?","value":"Hammam","group":"Historic Types","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its heated rooms continued and transformed older bathing traditions.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0461","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0461","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"What is the superposition of waves producing reinforcement or cancellation called?","value":"Interference","group":"Light Sound","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The relative phase determines the resulting amplitude.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0462","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0462","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What did the Suez Crisis demonstrate about Britain and France?","value":"Limits of their independent imperial power","group":"Postcolonial Context","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"International pressure forced a withdrawal after intervention in Egypt.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0463","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0463","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which Tuscan city developed influential banking networks under families such as the Bardi and Medici?","value":"Florence","group":"Mediterranean Trade","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Finance linked the city with courts and merchants across Europe.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0464","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0464","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Piedmontese city developed a regular Baroque extension as a Savoy capital?","value":"Turin","group":"Italian Urban History","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Royal planning connected streets, squares and court institutions.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0465","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0465","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which ornament consists of repeated small rectangular blocks beneath a cornice?","value":"Dentils","group":"Architectural Ornament","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The tooth-like series articulates the horizontal edge.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0466","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0466","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"A composition arranged along a clearly defined line of approach uses which organising principle?","value":"Axial planning","group":"Plan Types","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The axis links spaces and establishes visual direction.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0467","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0467","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which roof has two slopes on each side, with the lower slope steeper, and can enclose an attic storey?","value":"Mansard roof","group":"Roof Forms","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The form expands usable space beneath the roof.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0468","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0468","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which Athenian statesman was associated with the naval strategy at Salamis?","value":"Themistocles","group":"Greek People","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Athenian sea power was central to resistance against the Persian invasion.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0469","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0469","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which ornamental frame often surrounds an inscription or coat of arms?","value":"Cartouche","group":"Architectural Ornament","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its scrolling outline provides a distinct field for text or symbols.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0470","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0470","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Turin square is bounded by paired Baroque churches at one end?","value":"Piazza San Carlo","group":"Urban Spaces","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its regular architectural frame establishes a formal urban room.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0472","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0472","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which book by Venturi, Scott Brown and Izenour examined commercial roadside symbolism?","value":"Learning from Las Vegas","group":"Architectural Books","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It argued for attention to signs and ordinary urban environments.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0473","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0473","anchor":"MAJOR:GEOGRAPHY-AND-CIVICS","subject":"Which river flows through Lyon before reaching the Mediterranean?","value":"Rhône","group":"European Rivers","major":"Geography & Civics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its valley has long served as a major route through southeastern France.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0474","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0474","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The Great Schism conventionally dated to 1054 concerns which division?","value":"Eastern and Western Christianity","group":"Religious History","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The separation developed through a much longer history of disputes.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0475","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0475","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What was the significance of the Ruhr occupation in 1923?","value":"A crisis over German reparations","group":"Worldwar Context","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"French and Belgian occupation intensified the economic conflict.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0476","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0476","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes the crosswise arm intersecting a church's main longitudinal body?","value":"Transept","group":"Church","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It can give the plan the form of a cross.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0478","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0478","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Glasgow art school building combined Arts and Crafts influences with a distinctive modern spatial language?","value":"Glasgow School of Art","group":"Industrial Buildings","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Mackintosh's design responded to the needs of art education.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0479","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0479","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which battle is associated with Peter the Great's defeat of Charles XII of Sweden?","value":"Poltava","group":"Earlymodern Battles","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It shifted the balance of power in northern and eastern Europe.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0480","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0480","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which drawing records the actual completed construction rather than only the original proposal?","value":"As-built drawing","group":"Architectural Drawing","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It incorporates changes made during construction.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0481","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0481","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"What is the increase of a pollutant's concentration along a food chain called?","value":"Biomagnification","group":"Ecological Terms","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Persistent substances may become concentrated in higher-level consumers.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0482","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0482","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes masonry made from accurately cut blocks with regular faces?","value":"Ashlar","group":"Construction","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It contrasts with irregular rubble masonry.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0485","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0485","anchor":"MAJOR:GEOGRAPHY-AND-CIVICS","subject":"What is an enclosed depression formed by the collapse or dissolution of soluble rock called?","value":"Sinkhole","group":"Landforms","major":"Geography & Civics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It is a characteristic feature of karst landscapes.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0486","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0486","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which arch is built above an opening to divert loads away from the element below?","value":"Relieving arch","group":"Arch Types","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It reduces the load directly carried by a lintel or weaker opening.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0487","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0487","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Italian theorist wrote Teoria del restauro and helped shape modern conservation thought?","value":"Cesare Brandi","group":"Restoration People","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"His theory addresses the historical and aesthetic dimensions of an artwork.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0488","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0488","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architect transformed the ruins of Coventry Cathedral into a memorial beside a new cathedral?","value":"Basil Spence","group":"Restoration People","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The project kept the wartime ruins as a distinct historical presence.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0490","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0490","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"A building's internal arrangement freed from a grid of load-bearing walls exemplifies which concept?","value":"Free plan","group":"Plan Types","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"A separate structural frame allows more flexible partitions.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0491","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0491","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What did Algeria achieve through the Évian agreements?","value":"Independence from France","group":"Postcolonial Context","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The agreements followed a prolonged war.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0492","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0492","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which Italian maritime republic was a major rival of Venice in eastern Mediterranean commerce?","value":"Republic of Genoa","group":"Italian States","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Genoese networks also extended into the Black Sea.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0493","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0493","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Who was Julius Caesar's principal rival in the civil war culminating at Pharsalus?","value":"Pompey","group":"Roman People","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The struggle contributed to the collapse of republican government.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0495","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0495","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Roman church contains Andrea Pozzo's illusionistic ceiling of Saint Ignatius?","value":"Sant'Ignazio","group":"Baroque Buildings","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Painted architecture appears to extend the physical space upward.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0496","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0496","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which Pacific naval battle halted a major Japanese offensive in 1942?","value":"Midway","group":"Modern Battles","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Japan lost several fleet aircraft carriers.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0498","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0498","anchor":"MAJOR:GEOGRAPHY-AND-CIVICS","subject":"What is a river's branching depositional landform at its mouth called?","value":"Delta","group":"Landforms","major":"Geography & Civics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Sediment accumulates where river flow enters a larger body of water.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0499","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0499","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What was the principal objective of the Normandy landings?","value":"Opening a western front in occupied France","group":"Worldwar Context","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The operation supported the liberation of western Europe.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0500","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0500","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which French politician became emperor after first serving as president of the Second Republic?","value":"Napoleon III","group":"Nineteenth People","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"His rule established the Second Empire.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0501","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0501","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which battle in 1214 strengthened the position of the French king Philip II?","value":"Bouvines","group":"Medieval Battles","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The victory affected the balance among France, England and the Empire.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0502","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0502","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which family commissioned Borromini's work on Sant'Agnese in Agone under Innocent X?","value":"Pamphilj","group":"Renaissance Patronage","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The church forms part of the family's setting on Piazza Navona.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0503","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0503","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architect reconstructed Berlin's Neues Museum with new work visibly differentiated from surviving fabric?","value":"David Chipperfield","group":"Restoration People","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The project preserved traces of damage while restoring museum use.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0504","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0504","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which building type combined a tower with the residence of a medieval urban family?","value":"Tower house","group":"Historic Types","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Height expressed defence and status in many Italian towns.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0505","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0505","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which British reformer campaigned for the abolition of the slave trade?","value":"William Wilberforce","group":"Nineteenth People","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"He was a leading parliamentary figure in the abolitionist movement.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0506","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0506","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which British movement destroyed textile machinery as a protest against changing labour conditions?","value":"Luddism","group":"Social Movements","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The protests concerned livelihoods and employment practices, not simply hostility to technology.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0507","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0507","anchor":"MAJOR:DESIGN","subject":"Which process forces material through a die to produce a continuous cross-section?","value":"Extrusion","group":"Metalwork","major":"Design","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The resulting section remains consistent along its length.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0508","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0508","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Camillo Sitte book examined the artistic qualities of historic urban spaces?","value":"City Planning According to Artistic Principles","group":"Architectural Books","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It criticised aspects of contemporary planning through historical examples.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0509","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0509","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which concept describes growth on previously developed urban land rather than undeveloped countryside?","value":"Brownfield redevelopment","group":"Urban Models","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Reuse may require addressing contamination or obsolete infrastructure.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0511","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0511","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which planning approach concentrates development around public transport stations?","value":"Transit-oriented development","group":"Urban Models","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It connects density and mixed uses with access to transit.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0512","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0512","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Vitruvius' triad combines firmness and beauty with which third principle?","value":"Utility","group":"Architectural Theory","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The three principles connect structural soundness, use and appearance.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0513","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0513","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which battle outside Moscow caused enormous losses without destroying the Russian army?","value":"Borodino","group":"Napoleonic Battles","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The Russian army withdrew but remained a force in the campaign.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0514","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0514","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which European state ruled Eritrea as a colony before the Second World War?","value":"Italy","group":"Colonial Powers","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The territory became part of Italian colonial expansion in the Horn of Africa.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0515","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0515","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which US president announced the doctrine of containment in an address on aid to Greece and Turkey?","value":"Harry Truman","group":"Ww2 People","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The policy became a central element of the early Cold War.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0516","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0516","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes a large foundation slab distributing loads over a substantial area?","value":"Raft foundation","group":"Construction","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It can support several columns and walls together.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0519","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0519","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which process allowed photographic images to be fixed on silver-coated plates in the 1830s?","value":"Daguerreotype","group":"Industrial History","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The image was a unique object rather than a reproducible paper negative.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0520","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0520","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Palladian publication presents orders, houses, public buildings and ancient temples?","value":"The Four Books of Architecture","group":"Architectural Books","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The illustrated treatise helped transmit his architecture internationally.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0521","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0521","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"What is the formation of a solid from a solution during a chemical process called?","value":"Precipitation","group":"Chemistry Terms","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The insoluble solid is called a precipitate.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0522","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0522","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What body exercised emergency authority during the Reign of Terror?","value":"Committee of Public Safety","group":"Revolution Context","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It coordinated revolutionary government during internal and external crises.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0523","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0523","anchor":"MAJOR:GEOGRAPHY-AND-CIVICS","subject":"What is a projecting area of land surrounded by water on most sides called?","value":"Peninsula","group":"Landforms","major":"Geography & Civics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its remaining land connection distinguishes it from an island.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0524","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0524","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes the upper zone of windows above adjacent roofs or aisles?","value":"Clerestory","group":"Church","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its elevated position admits light into the central space.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0525","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0525","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Roman square was redesigned by Michelangelo with a trapezoidal arrangement?","value":"Piazza del Campidoglio","group":"Urban Spaces","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The design redirected the civic ensemble's orientation and visual focus.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0526","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0526","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes the upper slab of a classical capital?","value":"Abacus","group":"Classical","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It mediates between the capital below and the load above.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0527","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0527","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The assassination at Sarajevo directly precipitated which conflict?","value":"First World War","group":"Modern Events","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The July Crisis escalated through alliances and mobilisation.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0528","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0528","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which nineteenth-century building type gathered covered stalls for urban food distribution?","value":"Market hall","group":"Historic Types","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Iron and glass enabled large sheltered spaces.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0529","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0529","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"What is a 'bosquet' in a formal garden?","value":"A geometrically organised grove","group":"Landscape Forms","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Clipped trees can form enclosed outdoor rooms.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0530","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0530","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which European state controlled Brazil until its independence in 1822?","value":"Portugal","group":"Colonial Powers","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The royal court's transfer to Brazil shaped the path to independence.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0531","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0531","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What was a principal purpose of a princely studiolo?","value":"Private study and display of learning","group":"Renaissance Context","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Objects and images expressed the patron's intellectual interests.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0535","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0535","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"What is the region from which light cannot escape a black hole bounded by?","value":"Event horizon","group":"Astronomy Terms","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It marks a causal boundary rather than a material surface.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0536","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0536","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which English abbey became the principal setting of royal coronations?","value":"Westminster Abbey","group":"Gothic Buildings","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[{"file":"Map record","verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Westminster_Abbey","verificationStatus":"inherited_reference_locator_not_retrieved_this_pass","supportScope":"Building context; complete question claim still pending verification"}],"explanation74":"Its Gothic rebuilding was initiated under Henry III.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0537","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0537","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes the upper platform on which the columns of a Greek temple stand?","value":"Stylobate","group":"Classical","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It is the top step of the temple platform.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0538","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0538","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"What is the increase in vibration when a system is driven near its natural frequency called?","value":"Resonance","group":"Light Sound","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The effect is relevant to both musical instruments and structures.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0540","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0540","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which British suffrage campaigner founded the Women's Social and Political Union?","value":"Emmeline Pankhurst","group":"Nineteenth People","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The organisation adopted increasingly militant methods for women's voting rights.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0541","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0541","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which Athenian lawgiver is associated with the cancellation of debt bondage?","value":"Solon","group":"Greek People","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"His reforms addressed social conflict between debtors and creditors.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0542","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0542","anchor":"MAJOR:DESIGN","subject":"Which joint uses fan-shaped interlocking pins and tails?","value":"Dovetail joint","group":"Woodwork","major":"Design","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its geometry resists separation in the direction of the joint.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0543","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0543","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What was the 'cursus honorum'?","value":"A sequence of public offices","group":"Ancient Terms","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It structured the careers of Roman political elites.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0544","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0544","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What was Justinian's reconquest policy intended to restore?","value":"Imperial control of former western territories","group":"Roman Changes","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Campaigns recovered areas including Italy and North Africa.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0545","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0545","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The Treaty of Zaragoza supplemented Iberian agreements over which issue?","value":"Overseas spheres of influence","group":"Exploration","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It addressed claims in the eastern hemisphere.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0546","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0546","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"What does 'circulation' refer to in a building?","value":"Movement through connected spaces","group":"Architectural Theory","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Routes include corridors, stairs, ramps and other transitions.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0547","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0547","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Frank Lloyd Wright proposal imagined decentralised settlement linked by automobiles?","value":"Broadacre City","group":"Urban Models","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It offered an alternative to dense metropolitan concentration.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0548","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0548","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes the church area associated with clergy and singers near the sanctuary?","value":"Choir","group":"Church","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its location varies with the plan and liturgical tradition.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0549","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0549","anchor":"MAJOR:DESIGN","subject":"Which tendency proposed reducing form to essential geometries and avoiding unnecessary ornament?","value":"Minimalism","group":"Design Movements","major":"Design","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its meaning varies across design and the visual arts.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0551","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0551","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Carlo Scarpa project transformed a medieval Verona castle into a museum?","value":"Castelvecchio Museum","group":"Modern Buildings","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The intervention makes historical fabric and new display elements legible together.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0552","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0552","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What did the Opium Wars force China to accept?","value":"Expanded foreign commercial privileges","group":"Nineteenth Context","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Treaties opened ports and imposed other concessions.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0553","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0553","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Genoese palace is renowned for a hall of mirrors and belonged to the Balbi and Durazzo families?","value":"Palazzo Reale","group":"Italian Palaces","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its interiors preserve layers of aristocratic and royal occupation.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0554","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0554","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which French ruler was known as the 'Citizen King'?","value":"Louis Philippe","group":"Nineteenth People","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"His July Monarchy followed the overthrow of Charles X.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0555","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0555","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"In which region did the Phoenician cities of Tyre and Sidon develop?","value":"Levant","group":"Ancient Places","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Their coastal position supported maritime trade.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0556","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0556","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which settlement recognised the independence of the Dutch Republic from Spain?","value":"Peace of Münster","group":"Treaties","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It formed part of the wider Westphalian settlement.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0557","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0557","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which Habsburg ruler abolished serfdom's personal restrictions in several territories?","value":"Joseph II","group":"Earlymodern People","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"His reforms belong to the programme of enlightened absolutism.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0558","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0558","anchor":"MAJOR:DESIGN","subject":"Which technique creates geometric surface patterns from pieces of wood?","value":"Parquetry","group":"Woodwork","major":"Design","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It differs from the more pictorial uses common in marquetry.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0559","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0559","anchor":"MAJOR:DESIGN","subject":"Which process coats an object with a thin metal layer through an electric current?","value":"Electroplating","group":"Metalwork","major":"Design","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The method changes the surface without making the whole object from the coating metal.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0561","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0561","anchor":"MAJOR:GEOGRAPHY-AND-CIVICS","subject":"In which Italian region is the city of Mantua?","value":"Lombardy","group":"Italian Regions","major":"Geography & Civics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The Gonzaga court shaped its Renaissance heritage.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0562","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0562","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which castle on the Vomero hill stands beside the Certosa di San Martino and commands a view over Naples?","value":"Castel Sant'Elmo","group":"Italian Castles","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its elevated site gives it a strategic relationship with the urban landscape.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0563","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0563","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"What is a relationship in which both interacting species benefit called?","value":"Mutualism","group":"Biology Terms","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It is one type of ecological interaction.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0564","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0564","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which Portuguese port became a centre of the sea route to India?","value":"Lisbon","group":"Mediterranean Trade","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Asian commerce contributed to its early modern importance.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0565","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0565","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"Which international laboratory near Geneva is associated with particle accelerators and the development of the Web?","value":"CERN","group":"Scientific Landmarks","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its research investigates the fundamental constituents of matter.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0566","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0566","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes a system that heated floors and rooms by circulating hot air below them?","value":"Hypocaust","group":"Urban","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Roman baths are especially associated with this technology.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0568","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0568","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which dark fine-grained volcanic stone is common in paving and road construction?","value":"Basalt","group":"Stone Materials","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It forms from rapidly cooled lava.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0572","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0572","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"The conversion of the Gare d’Orsay retained which element of the former station as a dominant interior space?","value":"The long train shed","group":"Restoration People","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The former station hall became the museum’s principal longitudinal public space.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0573","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0573","anchor":"MAJOR:DESIGN","subject":"What is a product designed to serve people with different abilities without special adaptation an example of?","value":"Universal design","group":"Design Terms","major":"Design","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The approach aims to widen usability from the beginning of the design process.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0574","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0574","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Milan museum project by Studio BBPR placed displays within the Castello Sforzesco?","value":"Museum of Ancient Art at Castello Sforzesco","group":"Modern Italian Context","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The installation connected historical objects with a carefully designed visitor route.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0576","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0576","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"In which region was the ancient sanctuary of Olympia located?","value":"Elis","group":"Ancient Places","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The sanctuary hosted the ancient Olympic Games.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0577","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0577","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which fine-grained metamorphic stone splits into thin sheets suitable for roofing?","value":"Slate","group":"Stone Materials","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its cleavage supports the production of flat durable tiles.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0579","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0579","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which movement campaigned for the removal of legal disabilities affecting Jews in Europe?","value":"Jewish emancipation","group":"Social Movements","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The process developed unevenly across European states.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0580","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0580","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which London building by Barry and Pugin houses the national legislature in a Gothic Revival complex?","value":"Palace of Westminster","group":"European Civic Context","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The design followed the destruction of the earlier palace by fire.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0581","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0581","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which papal family gave its name to the Sistine Chapel through Pope Sixtus IV?","value":"Della Rovere","group":"Renaissance Patronage","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The chapel's later decoration involved several phases of patronage.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0582","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0582","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which dynasty ruled the Frankish kingdom before the Carolingians?","value":"Merovingians","group":"Medieval Dynasties","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The Carolingians first gained power as mayors of the palace.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0583","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0583","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which ornament resembles a suspended garland of fruit, flowers or leaves?","value":"Festoon","group":"Architectural Ornament","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It is often represented as hanging between two supports.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0585","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0585","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What was a central economic activity of Spanish Potosí?","value":"Silver mining","group":"Exploration","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The mines supplied global commercial networks through coerced labour.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0586","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0586","anchor":"MAJOR:GEOGRAPHY-AND-CIVICS","subject":"What is an isotherm on a map?","value":"A line of equal temperature","group":"Map Concepts","major":"Geography & Civics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It summarises spatial patterns in temperature.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0587","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0587","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Villa in Caprarola develops a pentagonal palace around a circular courtyard?","value":"Villa Farnese at Caprarola","group":"Italian Villas","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The form adapts the geometry of an earlier fortified project.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0588","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0588","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which event is associated with the term 'Biennio Rosso'?","value":"Postwar strikes and factory occupations","group":"Italian Social History","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Social conflict intensified in Italy after the First World War.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0589","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0589","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"What is a substance that accelerates a chemical reaction without being consumed overall called?","value":"Catalyst","group":"Chemistry Terms","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It changes the reaction pathway rather than the final equilibrium position.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0590","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0590","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which battle saw parliamentary forces defeat Charles I's main army in 1645?","value":"Naseby","group":"Earlymodern Battles","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The defeat seriously weakened the royalist position.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0591","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0591","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes vertical channels cut into a column shaft?","value":"Fluting","group":"Classical","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The grooves contribute to the articulation of the column surface.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0592","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0592","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"What is a sequence of aligned rooms with doorways forming a continuous vista called?","value":"Enfilade","group":"Spatial Terms","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It is common in palaces and some museum layouts.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0593","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0593","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What principle guided much of the Congress of Vienna's restoration of rulers?","value":"Dynastic legitimacy","group":"Nineteenth Context","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It was balanced against strategic interests and territorial bargaining.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0594","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0594","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which American document announced the colonies' separation from Britain?","value":"Declaration of Independence","group":"Historical Documents","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its political claims framed independence through rights and grievances.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0595","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0595","anchor":"MAJOR:GEOGRAPHY-AND-CIVICS","subject":"Which strait separates England from France at the Channel's narrowest point?","value":"Strait of Dover","group":"Waterways","major":"Geography & Civics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It links the English Channel with the North Sea.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0596","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0596","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which civilisation developed hieroglyphic writing along the Nile?","value":"Ancient Egyptians","group":"Ancient States","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Hieroglyphs appear in religious, royal and funerary settings.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0597","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0597","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which city became a major medieval centre for translating Arabic works into Latin in Iberia?","value":"Toledo","group":"Medieval Cities","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its multilingual setting supported intellectual exchange.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0600","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0600","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which episode brought Mussolini to the head of government in 1922?","value":"March on Rome","group":"Italian Social History","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The king's decision to appoint him was central to the outcome.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0601","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0601","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Tony Garnier proposal imagined a planned industrial settlement with separated functions?","value":"Cité Industrielle","group":"Urban Models","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Industry, housing and public facilities formed a coordinated urban scheme.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0602","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0602","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Kevin Lynch book introduced paths, edges, districts, nodes and landmarks as elements of urban perception?","value":"The Image of the City","group":"Architectural Books","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It examined how people form readable mental images of cities.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0603","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0603","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which arch has several repeated lobes along its inner edge?","value":"Multifoil arch","group":"Arch Types","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The lobed outline is often used decoratively.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0604","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0604","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which emperor is associated with the Sicilian court and the Constitutions of Melfi?","value":"Frederick II","group":"Medieval People","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"His rule combined southern Italian kingship with imperial ambitions.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0605","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0605","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"Which alloy consists principally of copper and tin?","value":"Bronze","group":"Materials Science","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its casting properties made it important in sculpture and tools.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0606","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0606","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The Spanish encomienda system primarily organised what?","value":"Colonial labour and tribute","group":"Exploration","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It imposed obligations on Indigenous communities.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0607","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0607","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which battle ended with Gustavus Adolphus' death despite a Swedish tactical success?","value":"Lützen","group":"Earlymodern Battles","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"His death removed a central leader of the Protestant coalition.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0609","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0609","anchor":"MAJOR:DESIGN","subject":"Which design tendency used flowing plant-like lines and integrated ornament around 1900?","value":"Art Nouveau","group":"Design Movements","major":"Design","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its regional variants shared a search for a new decorative language.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0610","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0610","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which ancient city contains the rock-cut façade known as Al-Khazneh?","value":"Petra","group":"Ancient Sites","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its architecture reflects Nabataean traditions and wider Mediterranean influences.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0611","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0611","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"What are atoms of the same element with different neutron numbers called?","value":"Isotopes","group":"Chemistry Terms","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"They share atomic number but differ in mass number.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0613","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0613","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which final Italian offensive in 1918 contributed to Austria-Hungary's collapse?","value":"Vittorio Veneto","group":"Modern Battles","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The victory coincided with the empire's political disintegration.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0614","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0614","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Pienza square brings together the cathedral, papal palace and civic buildings?","value":"Piazza Pio II","group":"Urban Spaces","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The compact ensemble expresses a coordinated Renaissance urban project.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0615","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0615","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Parisian museum extension by I. M. Pei uses a glass pyramid as a principal entrance?","value":"Louvre Pyramid","group":"Contemporary Buildings","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The intervention reorganised access to the historic museum complex.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0616","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0616","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Tuscan city converted its broad early modern ramparts into an elevated public promenade?","value":"Lucca","group":"Italian Urban History","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The defensive circuit became a landscape and recreational resource.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0617","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0617","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"Which instrument measures relative humidity?","value":"Hygrometer","group":"Scientific Instruments","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Humidity influences comfort and the risk of condensation.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0619","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0619","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which term describes control by a single supplier?","value":"monopoly","group":"Trade Economics","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The absence of direct competition can affect price and access.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0620","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0620","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"Which mineral is the main constituent of marble and limestone?","value":"Calcite","group":"Materials Science","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Their related chemistry does not mean that their formation or texture is identical.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0621","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0621","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Italian site contains Hadrian's extensive imperial villa?","value":"Tivoli","group":"Ancient Sites","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The complex combines varied architectural forms and landscape settings.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0622","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0622","anchor":"MAJOR:DESIGN","subject":"Which technique applies a thin decorative wood layer over a substrate?","value":"Veneering","group":"Woodwork","major":"Design","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It uses the visible qualities of one wood without requiring the entire object to be solid wood.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0623","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0623","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which tendency associated with Frampton argues for a modern architecture responsive to local conditions?","value":"Critical regionalism","group":"Modern Movements","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It resists both generic universalism and simple imitation of vernacular forms.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0625","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0625","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What was a major consequence of the Italian Wars begun in 1494?","value":"Greater foreign intervention in Italy","group":"Renaissance Context","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"French, Spanish and imperial ambitions reshaped the peninsula.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0626","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0626","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which city did Gabriele D'Annunzio occupy with his followers after the First World War?","value":"Fiume","group":"Italian Context","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The occupation became a prominent episode of postwar nationalist agitation.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0627","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0627","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"What is an atom or molecule with a net electrical charge called?","value":"Ion","group":"Chemistry Terms","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Charge results from a difference between the numbers of protons and electrons.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0628","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0628","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which building type developed around the storage, display and sale of varied goods under one management?","value":"Department store","group":"Historic Types","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It became a prominent feature of modern commercial cities.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0629","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0629","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Italian site is particularly known for three major Greek temples south of Salerno?","value":"Paestum","group":"Ancient Sites","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its surviving Doric temples belong to a Greek colonial setting.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0630","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0630","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Sicilian site contains the Valley of the Temples?","value":"Agrigento","group":"Ancient Sites","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The monumental sanctuary zone belonged to ancient Akragas.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0631","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0631","anchor":"MAJOR:DESIGN","subject":"What is a product's planned sequence from raw materials to disposal called in environmental assessment?","value":"Life cycle","group":"Design Terms","major":"Design","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The analysis includes production, use and end-of-life processes.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0633","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0633","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What did confessionalisation involve in early modern Europe?","value":"Closer organisation of religious and political life","group":"Reformation Context","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"States and churches promoted defined confessional identities.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0635","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0635","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What does archaeology principally investigate?","value":"Material remains of past societies","group":"Historical Sources","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its evidence extends beyond societies with written records.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0636","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0636","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"What term describes an organism's observable characteristics?","value":"Phenotype","group":"Biology Terms","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"They arise through interactions between genetic constitution and environment.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0637","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0637","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which Roman general is associated with the suppression of Spartacus' revolt?","value":"Crassus","group":"Roman People","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"He defeated the principal rebel army during the Third Servile War.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0638","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0638","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Paris railway station was converted into a museum of nineteenth-century art?","value":"Gare d'Orsay","group":"Architecture Adaptation","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The station's large interior accommodated a new cultural programme.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0639","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0639","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Roman decorative technique forms designs from cut pieces of coloured stone?","value":"Opus sectile","group":"Roman Construction","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The pieces follow the shapes of the design rather than a uniform tessera grid.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0640","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0640","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes a basin in a Roman atrium that collected rainwater?","value":"Impluvium","group":"Urban","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It lay below the roof opening known as the compluvium.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0641","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0641","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What was the principal purpose of wartime rationing?","value":"Allocation of scarce essential goods","group":"Worldwar Context","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It sought to manage shortages and sustain the war effort.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0642","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0642","anchor":"MAJOR:DESIGN","subject":"What is the deliberate design of products to become outdated or unusable relatively quickly called?","value":"Planned obsolescence","group":"Design Terms","major":"Design","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It can involve technical limits, incompatibility or fashion-driven replacement.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0643","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0643","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes a continuous foundation beneath a load-bearing wall?","value":"Strip foundation","group":"Construction","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It distributes the wall's load along a line.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0645","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0645","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"What is a building's 'programme' in architectural design?","value":"Its required activities and spaces","group":"Architectural Theory","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The programme sets functional requirements rather than a decorative style.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0646","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0646","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What was a principal role of diplomatic residents in Renaissance Italian states?","value":"Continuous representation at foreign courts","group":"Renaissance Context","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"They gathered information and maintained political relationships.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0647","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0647","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What is 'urbanisation'?","value":"Growth of urban populations","group":"Historical Concepts","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Industrialisation accelerated it in many European societies.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0648","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0648","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which Milanese dynasty commissioned Leonardo's Last Supper during Ludovico's rule?","value":"Sforza","group":"Renaissance Patronage","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The commission formed part of a wider project at Santa Maria delle Grazie.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0650","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0650","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"What is the maintenance of relatively stable internal conditions called?","value":"Homeostasis","group":"Biology Terms","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Regulatory systems respond to changing external and internal conditions.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0651","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0651","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Roman complex by Michelangelo reused the ancient Baths of Diocletian for a church?","value":"Santa Maria degli Angeli e dei Martiri","group":"Italian Civic Buildings","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The adaptation retained the scale of parts of the Roman bath structure.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0652","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0652","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Roman Renaissance palace became the long-standing seat of the French embassy in Italy?","value":"Palazzo Farnese","group":"Italian Palaces","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its later diplomatic role follows its origin as an aristocratic residence.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0653","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0653","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What was a principal result of the Edict of Milan?","value":"Legal toleration of Christianity","group":"Roman Changes","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It did not make Christianity the empire's official religion.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0654","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0654","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which Flemish city was a major medieval trading centre before Antwerp's rise?","value":"Bruges","group":"Mediterranean Trade","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its commercial importance depended partly on access to maritime routes.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0656","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0656","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes a small chapel projecting around an ambulatory or apse?","value":"Radiating chapel","group":"Church","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Such chapels are characteristic of many pilgrimage churches.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0658","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0658","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"What term describes an organism's functional role within an ecosystem?","value":"Ecological niche","group":"Ecological Terms","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The role includes its resource use and interactions with other organisms.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0660","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0660","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which machine transformed nineteenth-century newspaper and book production through powered printing?","value":"Steam-powered printing press","group":"Industrial History","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Mechanical power increased printing capacity beyond hand presses.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0661","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0661","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"What does 'facadism' usually describe?","value":"Retention of a façade with major rebuilding behind","group":"Architectural Theory","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The practice raises questions about the depth of architectural preservation.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0662","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0662","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which movement is associated with Taut's Glass Pavilion and emotionally charged crystalline forms?","value":"Expressionism","group":"Modern Movements","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Architectural form was treated as an expressive rather than purely rational vehicle.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0663","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0663","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"In which region did the ancient city of Babylon develop?","value":"Mesopotamia","group":"Ancient Places","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It stood on the Euphrates in present-day Iraq.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0664","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0664","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What is an anachronism?","value":"A misplaced feature from another time","group":"Historical Sources","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It can distort historical representation or interpretation.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0666","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0666","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which term describes a tax on traded goods?","value":"tariff","group":"Trade Economics","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Governments can use tariffs to raise revenue or protect domestic production.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0667","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0667","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What administrative change is associated with Constantine's rebuilding of Byzantium?","value":"Creation of a new imperial capital","group":"Roman Changes","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Constantinople became the centre of the eastern empire.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0668","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0668","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Ivrea building by Figini and Pollini expanded Olivetti's industrial facilities with a modern glazed façade?","value":"Olivetti ICO workshops","group":"Modern Italian Context","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The factories formed part of a wider programme linking industry and social design.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0669","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0669","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Sicilian site preserves a large unfinished Doric temple and a hillside theatre?","value":"Segesta","group":"Ancient Sites","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The temple and theatre belong to different phases of the settlement.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0670","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0670","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which naval battle ended with Nelson's death and a British victory over the Franco-Spanish fleet?","value":"Trafalgar","group":"Napoleonic Battles","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The victory secured British naval superiority without ending the continental war.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0671","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0671","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes the ensemble of choir, apse, ambulatory and chapels at a church's eastern end?","value":"Chevet","group":"Church","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The term describes the overall eastern termination.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0672","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0672","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What was a medieval 'scriptorium'?","value":"A manuscript-copying workshop","group":"Medieval Terms","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Monastic scribes preserved and produced written texts there.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0673","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0673","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which structure formed the monumental entrance to the Athenian Acropolis?","value":"Propylaea","group":"Ancient Buildings","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It organised the transition from the approach to the sacred precinct.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0674","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0674","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Neapolitan museum palace was originally a Bourbon royal residence on a hill?","value":"Palace of Capodimonte","group":"Italian Palaces","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The building later became a major setting for art collections.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0675","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0675","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"At which battle did Athenian forces defeat a Persian landing army before the invasion of Xerxes?","value":"Marathon","group":"Ancient Battles","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The victory became a major part of Athenian civic memory.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0676","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0676","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which ornament takes the form of a stylised human or animal face?","value":"Mascaron","group":"Architectural Ornament","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It can decorate keystones, fountains and other architectural elements.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0677","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0677","anchor":"MAJOR:GEOGRAPHY-AND-CIVICS","subject":"What is a steep-sided valley flooded by the sea after glacial erosion called?","value":"Fjord","group":"Landforms","major":"Geography & Civics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its submerged profile reflects former glacier movement.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0679","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0679","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Roman port city near the Tiber mouth preserves extensive apartment buildings and mosaics?","value":"Ostia Antica","group":"Ancient Sites","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The site illustrates urban life connected with Rome's maritime supply.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0680","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0680","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What does 'enclosure' describe in British agrarian history?","value":"Consolidation of land into private holdings","group":"Historical Concepts","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The process altered access to common land and patterns of rural labour.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0681","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0681","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The invasion of Poland by Nazi Germany opened which European conflict?","value":"Second World War","group":"Modern Events","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Britain and France then declared war on Germany.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0682","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0682","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which system embeds steel to resist tensile forces within a material strong in compression?","value":"Reinforced concrete","group":"Structural Systems","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The materials perform complementary structural roles.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0683","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0683","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which emperor's reign included the destruction of Pompeii by Vesuvius?","value":"Titus","group":"Roman People","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The eruption occurred in 79 CE, shortly after he succeeded Vespasian.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0684","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0684","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which agreement divided Spanish and Portuguese claims to newly encountered lands along an Atlantic meridian?","value":"Treaty of Tordesillas","group":"Treaties","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The agreement reflected Iberian competition over overseas expansion.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0685","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0685","anchor":"MAJOR:DESIGN","subject":"What is the deliberate reduction of unnecessary material in a product's design called?","value":"Material efficiency","group":"Design Terms","major":"Design","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It considers performance relative to the resources used.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0686","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0686","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes construction using irregular or roughly dressed stones?","value":"Rubble masonry","group":"Construction","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Mortar and packing accommodate the stones' varying forms.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0687","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0687","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which French king was captured during a crusade in Egypt?","value":"Louis IX","group":"Medieval People","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"He is also known as Saint Louis.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0688","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0688","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Venetian fortress town is recognised for its radial star-shaped plan?","value":"Palmanova","group":"Italian Urban History","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The geometry responds to military defence as well as planned urban organisation.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0689","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0689","anchor":"MAJOR:GEOGRAPHY-AND-CIVICS","subject":"What does a population-density map compare?","value":"People per unit area","group":"Map Concepts","major":"Geography & Civics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"A large population does not necessarily imply high density.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0691","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0691","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What did the principle sola scriptura emphasise?","value":"The authority of scripture","group":"Reformation Context","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It challenged the relationship between biblical text and church tradition.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0692","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0692","anchor":"MAJOR:DESIGN","subject":"Which interwar tendency adapted aerodynamic forms to products that did not necessarily need to move?","value":"Streamlining","group":"Design Movements","major":"Design","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Speed became a visual metaphor for modernity.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0693","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0693","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Parisian library by Henri Labrouste exposes a slender iron framework in its reading room?","value":"Bibliothèque Sainte-Geneviève","group":"Industrial Buildings","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The interior combines modern structural technology with a monumental public programme.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0694","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0694","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What did Augustus' settlement of power preserve in outward form?","value":"Republican institutions","group":"Roman Changes","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Monarchical authority developed behind retained republican offices.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0696","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0696","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which Italian city was devastated by Frederick Barbarossa and later rebuilt with Lombard support?","value":"Milan","group":"Medieval Cities","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The conflict formed part of struggles over imperial and communal power.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0697","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0697","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What was the primary role of Roman tribunes of the plebs?","value":"Protection of plebeian interests","group":"Ancient Terms","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Their powers included intervention against actions of other magistrates.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0699","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0699","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Florentine civic palace is crowned by the Tower of Arnolfo?","value":"Palazzo Vecchio","group":"Italian Civic Buildings","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its fortified appearance expresses communal authority.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0701","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0701","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes a small structure crowning a dome and admitting light?","value":"Lantern","group":"Structure","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It can also form a prominent feature of the external silhouette.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0702","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0702","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which Italian victory helped Napoleon consolidate the Consulate in 1800?","value":"Marengo","group":"Napoleonic Battles","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The battle restored French control over much of northern Italy.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0703","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0703","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which Japanese ruling house controlled the shogunate from Edo?","value":"Tokugawa house","group":"World Culture","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its rule established a long period of political order before the Meiji transformation.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0704","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0704","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"Which Florentine experimental academy was associated with the motto 'trying and trying again'?","value":"Accademia del Cimento","group":"Scientific Landmarks","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its work emphasised experimental investigation.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0706","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0706","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which pharaoh's tomb was discovered by Howard Carter?","value":"Tutankhamun","group":"Ancient Rulers","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The relatively intact burial provided exceptional evidence of royal funerary culture.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0707","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0707","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which European state ruled most of India through the Raj?","value":"Great Britain","group":"Colonial Powers","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Direct crown rule followed the East India Company's government.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0708","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0708","anchor":"MAJOR:DESIGN","subject":"What is the repeated production of identical standard parts called?","value":"Mass production","group":"Design Terms","major":"Design","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Standardisation makes assembly and replacement more efficient.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0709","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0709","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Luther's initial controversy over indulgences concerned what?","value":"Remission of penalties for sin","group":"Reformation Context","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The dispute expanded into wider challenges to church authority.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0711","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0711","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes a thickened or projecting end of a wall in a classical building?","value":"Anta","group":"Classical","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Columns placed between such wall ends form an in-antis arrangement.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0712","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0712","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which author analysed princely power in Il Principe?","value":"Niccolò Machiavelli","group":"Political Thought","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The work examines political action through historical and contemporary examples.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0714","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0714","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which movement linked nineteenth-century cooperative experiments with alternatives to industrial capitalism?","value":"Utopian socialism","group":"Social Movements","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The label encompasses differing social proposals and communities.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0716","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0716","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which movement sought closer cultural and political unity among Slavic peoples?","value":"Pan-Slavism","group":"Social Movements","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its meanings varied among states and national movements.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0717","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0717","anchor":"MAJOR:DESIGN","subject":"What is a simplified graphic sign representing an object or action called?","value":"Pictogram","group":"Graphic Design","major":"Design","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its communication depends on recognisable visual conventions.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0719","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0719","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"What is the diffusion of water through a selectively permeable membrane called?","value":"Osmosis","group":"Biology Terms","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Water movement depends on differences in chemical potential.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0720","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0720","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which city hosted the oldest university traditionally dated to 1088?","value":"Bologna","group":"Medieval Cities","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its early reputation was strongly connected with legal studies.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0721","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0721","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Who unified Macedonia and defeated the Greek alliance at Chaeronea?","value":"Philip II","group":"Ancient Rulers","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The victory prepared the expansion later led by his son Alexander.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0722","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0722","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Jane Jacobs book criticised large-scale urban renewal and defended mixed city life?","value":"The Death and Life of Great American Cities","group":"Architectural Books","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It emphasised everyday activity and the social organisation of streets.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0723","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0723","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The Montefeltro court was based in which Renaissance state?","value":"Duchy of Urbino","group":"Italian States","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Federico da Montefeltro became a celebrated patron of the arts.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0724","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0724","anchor":"MAJOR:DESIGN","subject":"Which nineteenth-century approach freely combined motifs from different historical styles?","value":"Eclecticism","group":"Design Movements","major":"Design","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Selection and combination were central to its design practice.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0726","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0726","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Lombard town was planned as a ducal capital by Vespasiano Gonzaga?","value":"Sabbioneta","group":"Italian Urban History","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its urban form expresses Renaissance ideals within a small fortified settlement.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0727","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0727","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"Which Oxford museum developed from a collection that included the Tradescant cabinet of curiosities?","value":"Ashmolean Museum","group":"Scientific Landmarks","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It is an early example of a public university museum.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0728","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0728","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What was the Italian Resistance principally directed against during 1943–45?","value":"Nazi occupation and Fascist rule","group":"Italian Social History","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its participants included diverse political and social groups.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0729","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0729","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"What is a recess deep enough to form a subsidiary space within a room called?","value":"Alcove","group":"Spatial Terms","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It may accommodate a bed, seat or other specific use.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0730","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0730","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Adriatic city grew within and around Diocletian's palace?","value":"Split","group":"Ancient Sites","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Later urban development reused the fortified imperial complex.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0733","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0733","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"Which Italian institution founded in 1603 counted Galileo among its members?","value":"Accademia dei Lincei","group":"Scientific Landmarks","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its name evokes the sharp sight of the lynx.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0734","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0734","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"A church with arms of approximately equal length has which plan type?","value":"Greek cross","group":"Plan Types","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The arrangement differs from the elongated Latin cross.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0735","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0735","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The iconoclastic controversy in Byzantium concerned which issue?","value":"Veneration of religious images","group":"Religious History","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Debate focused on the legitimacy and use of sacred representations.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0737","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0737","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which German city was particularly associated with Charlemagne's palace complex?","value":"Aachen","group":"Medieval Cities","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The palace chapel remains a major Carolingian monument.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0738","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0738","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which movement linked Walter Gropius' school with the integration of art, craft and industry?","value":"Bauhaus","group":"Modern Movements","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its educational programme changed during the school's different phases.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0740","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0740","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"What process wears away and transports soil or rock by water, wind or ice?","value":"Erosion","group":"Earth Processes","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It differs from weathering, which breaks material down in place.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0741","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0741","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which classical moulding alternates oval forms with pointed elements?","value":"Egg-and-dart","group":"Architectural Ornament","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its repeated units enrich the profile of a moulding.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0743","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0743","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What did public museums change in the relationship between collections and society?","value":"Access beyond private court circles","group":"Intellectual Context","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Public access developed gradually and remained shaped by institutions.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0744","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0744","anchor":"MAJOR:GEOGRAPHY-AND-CIVICS","subject":"Which channel separates mainland Italy from the island of Elba?","value":"Piombino Channel","group":"Waterways","major":"Geography & Civics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The passage lies off the Tuscan coast.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0745","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0745","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which German industrial region is associated with the Zollverein coal-mine cultural complex?","value":"Ruhr","group":"Architecture Adaptation","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Industrial heritage became a resource for regional transformation.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0746","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0746","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"What phenomenon produces water droplets when humid air contacts a sufficiently cold surface?","value":"Condensation","group":"Building Physics","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The surface temperature has fallen below the air's dew point.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0747","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0747","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"What is the alignment of a light wave's oscillations in a particular orientation called?","value":"Polarisation","group":"Light Sound","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Polarising filters select particular orientations.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0748","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0748","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What was the assignat originally backed by?","value":"Confiscated church property","group":"Revolution Context","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its later overissue contributed to monetary instability.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0749","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0749","anchor":"MAJOR:DESIGN","subject":"Which surface treatment mechanically removes wood to create decorative relief?","value":"Carving","group":"Woodwork","major":"Design","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The design is formed by subtraction rather than applied ornament.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0750","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0750","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Vienna postal bank building uses aluminium details and an innovative banking hall?","value":"Austrian Postal Savings Bank","group":"Industrial Buildings","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Otto Wagner connected modern materials with a rational institutional programme.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0752","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0752","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"Which Paris institution was founded under Louis XIV to organise scientific work?","value":"Académie des sciences","group":"Scientific Landmarks","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It became an important part of state-supported scientific culture.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0753","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0753","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes a framework commonly using triangles to span an opening?","value":"Truss","group":"Structure","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The triangular arrangement helps stabilize the assembly.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0754","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0754","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Urbino palace contains a famous studiolo decorated with perspective wood inlay?","value":"Ducal Palace of Urbino","group":"Italian Palaces","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The room presents learning through illusionistically represented objects.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0755","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0755","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which concept associated with Clarence Perry organised housing around local facilities and an elementary school?","value":"Neighbourhood unit","group":"Urban Models","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The model separated local residential life from major through traffic.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0757","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0757","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which London insurance headquarters by Richard Rogers externalises lifts and service towers?","value":"Lloyd's Building","group":"Contemporary Buildings","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its arrangement frees the main interior for a large underwriting space.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0759","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0759","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"What term describes an experiment that can be repeated with consistent results?","value":"Reproducible experiment","group":"Scientific Methods","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Reproducibility supports the reliability of a scientific claim.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0760","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0760","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which soft, fine-grained stone used for carving may consist of gypsum or calcite?","value":"Alabaster","group":"Stone Materials","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The name covers two different mineral materials used decoratively.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0763","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0763","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which European state colonised the territory that became Algeria?","value":"France","group":"Colonial Powers","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Settlement and legal inequality became central features of colonial rule.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0765","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0765","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"Which technology converts sunlight directly into electricity?","value":"Photovoltaic cells","group":"Energy Sources","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The conversion depends on the electronic properties of semiconductor materials.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0766","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0766","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"A contemporary diary is usually classified as what kind of historical source?","value":"Primary source","group":"Historical Sources","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It provides evidence from the period, though its account still requires criticism.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0768","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0768","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes a pediment deliberately interrupted at the apex or base?","value":"Broken pediment","group":"Facade","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The device appears in Renaissance and especially Baroque design.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0769","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0769","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What was abolished during the French National Assembly's August decrees?","value":"Feudal privileges","group":"Revolution Context","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The process involved complex distinctions over dues and compensation.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0770","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0770","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which Chinese dynasty ruled immediately before the republic established in 1912?","value":"Qing dynasty","group":"World Culture","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its collapse ended the imperial political system.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0771","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0771","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What did the term virtù often imply in Machiavelli's political writing?","value":"Capacity for effective political action","group":"Renaissance Context","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It cannot simply be equated with conventional moral virtue.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0772","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0772","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Barcelona concert hall by Domènech i Montaner is known for a luminous stained-glass skylight?","value":"Palau de la Música Catalana","group":"European Civic Context","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Decoration and structure contribute to a strong civic cultural identity.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0773","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0773","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What was a principal role of chartered East India companies?","value":"Monopolised overseas trade","group":"Exploration","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Some also acquired military and territorial powers.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0774","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0774","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes a room traditionally opening off the atrium of a Roman house for reception or business?","value":"Tablinum","group":"Urban","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its position linked household display and formal social activity.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0775","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0775","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which drawing separates components while retaining their spatial relationships?","value":"Exploded view","group":"Architectural Drawing","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It clarifies how parts fit together.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0776","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0776","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Italian architect proposed principles distinguishing new restoration work from original fabric in the nineteenth century?","value":"Camillo Boito","group":"Restoration People","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"His approach sought to respect historical evidence while permitting necessary intervention.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0777","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0777","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which British group proposed speculative projects such as Plug-In City?","value":"Archigram","group":"Architecture Groups","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its drawings used technological and popular imagery to rethink architecture.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0778","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0778","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which writing system did the Romans adapt principally through Etruscan mediation?","value":"Alphabet derived from Greek","group":"Ancient States","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The Latin alphabet developed through the Etruscan adaptation of a Greek alphabet.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0779","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0779","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"Which mode of heat transfer requires direct interaction within a material?","value":"Conduction","group":"Building Physics","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Heat passes through matter without bulk movement of that material.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0780","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0780","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The Ninety-five Theses are associated with which movement?","value":"Protestant Reformation","group":"Religious History","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The controversy initially focused on indulgences.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0781","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0781","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which southern Italian city became the seat of the Norman kings of Sicily?","value":"Palermo","group":"Medieval Cities","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its court brought several cultural traditions into contact.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0782","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0782","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"What is the change from solid directly to gas called?","value":"Sublimation","group":"Chemistry Terms","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The liquid state is bypassed under the relevant conditions.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0783","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0783","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes a three-part opening with a central arch flanked by lower rectangular openings?","value":"Serliana","group":"Facade","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The motif is also known as a Palladian or Venetian window.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0785","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0785","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which philosopher associated the greatest happiness principle with utilitarianism?","value":"Jeremy Bentham","group":"Political Thought","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The principle evaluates actions through their consequences for happiness.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0786","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0786","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What was the Senate under the Roman Republic?","value":"A council of leading magistrates and former magistrates","group":"Ancient Terms","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its political authority was considerable despite changes over time.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0787","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0787","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"In which region did the ancient city of Thebes stand beside the Nile?","value":"Upper Egypt","group":"Ancient Places","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It was a major royal and religious centre.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0788","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0788","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"What is the return of light or sound from a surface called?","value":"Reflection","group":"Light Sound","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The geometry of the surface influences the direction of the returned wave.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0790","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0790","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which arch curves through more than a semicircle before returning to its supports?","value":"Horseshoe arch","group":"Arch Types","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The form appears in several pre-Islamic and Islamic traditions.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0791","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0791","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What was the cahier de doléances used to record?","value":"Grievances for the Estates-General","group":"Revolution Context","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The notebooks gathered demands before the assembly met.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0792","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0792","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which roof includes vegetation over a layered waterproofing and drainage system?","value":"Green roof","group":"Roof Forms","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The planting requires an appropriate structural and environmental system.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0793","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0793","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Roman wall construction combines bands of different facing materials?","value":"Opus mixtum","group":"Roman Construction","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The arrangement can alternate brick and stone treatments.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0794","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0794","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Ravenna church has a long nave mosaic showing a procession of female saints?","value":"Sant'Apollinare Nuovo","group":"Church Features","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its decoration reflects changes from Ostrogothic to Byzantine rule.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0795","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0795","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes a roofed porch supported by columns?","value":"Portico","group":"Facade","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It commonly emphasizes the entrance to a building.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0797","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0797","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"Which mode of heat transfer can occur through a vacuum?","value":"Radiation","group":"Building Physics","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Electromagnetic waves carry energy without requiring a material medium.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0798","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0798","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"What is an exterior platform projecting from an upper floor called?","value":"Balcony","group":"Spatial Terms","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its relationship to structure and enclosure differs from an interior gallery.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0800","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0800","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"At which battle did Constantine defeat Maxentius near Rome?","value":"Milvian Bridge","group":"Ancient Battles","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The victory consolidated his authority in the western empire.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0801","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0801","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What does 'serfdom' describe?","value":"Dependent rural labour tied to an estate","group":"Medieval Terms","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its legal and economic forms varied across regions.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0802","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0802","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which designer helped found the Society for the Protection of Ancient Buildings?","value":"William Morris","group":"Restoration People","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The society opposed speculative restoration and advocated conservative repair.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0804","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0804","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes a building intended especially for musical performances and related events in antiquity?","value":"Odeon","group":"Urban","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It was generally smaller than a large open-air theatre.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0806","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0806","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"What process releases usable energy from organic compounds within cells?","value":"Cellular respiration","group":"Biology Terms","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It is not the same process as breathing air into the lungs.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0807","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0807","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which family built a major Renaissance palace in Rome later frescoed by Annibale Carracci?","value":"Farnese","group":"Renaissance Patronage","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The palace became a prominent centre of aristocratic patronage.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0808","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0808","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes a classical order extending through more than one storey?","value":"Giant order","group":"Facade","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It unifies several levels within a single column or pilaster system.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0810","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0810","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes a projecting semicircular or polygonal termination of a church?","value":"Apse","group":"Church","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It commonly accommodates the sanctuary at the liturgical east end.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0812","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0812","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"In which region was the ancient city of Syracuse founded?","value":"Sicily","group":"Ancient Places","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It became a major Greek city in the central Mediterranean.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0813","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0813","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"What is an 'allée' in garden design?","value":"A tree-lined avenue","group":"Landscape Forms","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It establishes a directional route or vista.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0814","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0814","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Milan skyscraper by Gio Ponti and collaborators was built as Pirelli's headquarters?","value":"Pirelli Tower","group":"Modern Italian Context","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its slender plan and tapered ends create a distinctive office-tower form.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0815","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0815","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which simplified drawing emphasises relationships or processes rather than exact appearance?","value":"Diagram","group":"Architectural Drawing","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its selective abstraction makes a particular idea easier to understand.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0816","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0816","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes the outer curved surface of an arch?","value":"Extrados","group":"Structure","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It lies opposite the intrados.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0817","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0817","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which movement demanded the union of Italian territories under a common national state?","value":"Risorgimento","group":"Social Movements","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Republican, monarchical and federal projects competed within it.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0818","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0818","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Roman monument's relief spiral narrates campaigns in Dacia?","value":"Trajan's Column","group":"Ancient Buildings","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The continuous relief links imperial commemoration with military narrative.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0819","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0819","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"What is a transitional space between an entrance and a main interior called?","value":"Vestibule","group":"Spatial Terms","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It can mediate circulation, security and environmental conditions.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0820","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0820","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Roman palace includes Borromini's forced-perspective colonnade?","value":"Palazzo Spada","group":"Baroque Buildings","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Diminishing dimensions make the short passage appear much longer.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0821","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0821","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which city hosted the treaty ending the Third Italian War of Independence in 1866?","value":"Vienna","group":"Italian Context","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The settlement resulted in the transfer of Venetia to Italy.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0822","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0822","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What does epigraphy study?","value":"Inscriptions","group":"Historical Sources","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The material setting and letter forms help interpret written records.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0823","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0823","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Roman mosaic technique uses exceptionally small tesserae following the contours of a design?","value":"Opus vermiculatum","group":"Roman Construction","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The fine scale supports detailed modelling and outlines.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0824","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0824","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which Italian defeat in 1917 led to a retreat to the Piave line?","value":"Caporetto","group":"Modern Battles","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The breakthrough triggered major military and political changes.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0825","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0825","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What is 'secularisation'?","value":"Declining religious control of social institutions","group":"Historical Concepts","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The process varies across societies and does not imply the disappearance of belief.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0826","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0826","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"What does the term 'Years of Lead' refer to in Italian history?","value":"Political violence and terrorism","group":"Italian Social History","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The period involved attacks by groups with different political orientations.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0827","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0827","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"What is 'anastylosis' in conservation?","value":"Reassembly of original dismembered elements","group":"Architectural Theory","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The method is particularly associated with archaeological monuments.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0828","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0828","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes a continuous row of columns supporting a horizontal or arched structure?","value":"Colonnade","group":"Facade","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It organizes both circulation and architectural rhythm.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0829","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0829","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which reformer proposed an agrarian redistribution programme before being killed in 133 BCE?","value":"Tiberius Gracchus","group":"Roman People","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Conflict over public land was central to his tribunate.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0830","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0830","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which infrastructure carried coal and goods by water before railway expansion?","value":"Canal network","group":"Industrial History","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Canals connected production centres with markets and ports.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0831","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0831","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which English cathedral is associated with the pilgrimage shrine of Thomas Becket?","value":"Canterbury Cathedral","group":"Gothic Buildings","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[{"file":"Map record","verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canterbury_Cathedral","verificationStatus":"inherited_reference_locator_not_retrieved_this_pass","supportScope":"Building context; complete question claim still pending verification"}],"explanation74":"The cult of the murdered archbishop brought pilgrims to the cathedral.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0832","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0832","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which dynasty ruled England after Henry VII's victory at Bosworth?","value":"Tudors","group":"Medieval Dynasties","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The victory ended the main phase of the Wars of the Roses.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0835","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0835","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which roof consists of a single sloping plane?","value":"Shed roof","group":"Roof Forms","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It is also called a mono-pitch roof.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0836","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0836","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which English statesman led the republican Commonwealth after the Civil War?","value":"Oliver Cromwell","group":"Earlymodern People","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"He later ruled as Lord Protector.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0837","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0837","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The Five Days uprising challenged Austrian authority in which city?","value":"Milan","group":"Italian Context","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It was part of the revolutionary upheavals of 1848.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0838","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0838","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which dynasty ruled China when the terracotta army was created for its first emperor?","value":"Qin dynasty","group":"World Culture","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The figures formed part of a vast funerary complex.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0840","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0840","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which arch has a nearly flat lower edge while retaining wedge-shaped voussoirs?","value":"Flat arch","group":"Arch Types","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its joint geometry distinguishes it from a monolithic lintel.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0841","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0841","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"At which battle did Alexander decisively defeat Darius III in Mesopotamia?","value":"Gaugamela","group":"Ancient Battles","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The victory opened the Persian imperial heartland to conquest.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0842","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0842","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which Venetian building combined the residence of the doge with governmental and judicial spaces?","value":"Doge's Palace","group":"Italian Palaces","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Its architecture accommodated the institutions of the republic.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0843","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0843","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Knossos was a major palace centre of which civilisation?","value":"Minoan civilisation","group":"Ancient States","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The palace belongs to Bronze Age Crete.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0845","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0845","anchor":"MAJOR:SCIENCE-AND-TECH","subject":"What is the point in an orbit nearest the Sun called?","value":"Perihelion","group":"Astronomy Terms","major":"Science & Tech","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The corresponding farthest point is aphelion.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0847","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0847","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"Which architectural term denotes a deliberate separation allowing parts of a building to move without damaging one another?","value":"Expansion joint","group":"Construction","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"Movement can result from temperature changes and other effects.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0849","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0849","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Which agreement is associated with the beginning of European Union citizenship?","value":"Treaty of Maastricht","group":"Treaties","major":"History & Politics","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"It also established the European Union and a path towards monetary union.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0850","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0850","anchor":"MAJOR:ARCHITECTURE","subject":"A town organised by intersecting streets at right angles has which plan type?","value":"Orthogonal grid","group":"Plan Types","major":"Architecture","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The grid can support regular blocks and clear division of land.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0853","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0853","anchor":"MAJOR:DESIGN","subject":"What is a system made from standard units that can be combined in different arrangements called?","value":"Modular system","group":"Design Terms","major":"Design","relation":"review question","references":[],"explanation74":"The same components can support varied configurations.","previewOnly95":false,"review101":"editorially_reviewed"},{"id":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0854","nodeId":"REVIEW99-ARCHED-NEW99-0854","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTOR